\par\par \b \uc2 Another Bad Day for Emerging Markets -- Barron's Blog\b0\par\par\uc2 By Johanna Bennett  \par \uc2 485 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 November 2014\par 17:32\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 While the willingness of Europe's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to take more steps to stimulate growth has boosted European stocks, it isn't doing much to help emerging markets.\par \par \uc2 The MSCI Emerging Markets Index lost 0.7% to 991.61 at 10:27 a.m. in New York, its fourth day of declines. The \uc2 iShares MSCI Emerging Markets ETF\uc2  ( EEM) fell 0.68% to $41.19.\par \par \uc2 ISI Evercore strategists Dennis DeBusschere and Brian Herlihy wrote in a note published this morning:\par \par \uc2 With commodity prices still falling and Europe, a major importer of EM goods, slowing, many emerging markets are likely to see additional weakness in economic growth. Much of the emerging world, which is suffering from a combination of higher inflation and falling growth will be unable to stimulate in the way the U.S., China and, hopefully soon, Europe have. We continue to favor U.S. focused risk, especially non-commodity related assets.\par \par \uc2 ECB President \uc2 Mario Draghi\uc2  faces pressure to do more to support a slowing Eurozone economy after the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  last week unexpectedly boosted its stimulus plan.\par \par \uc2 The ECB kept interest rates unchanged today. No big surprise there. But Draghi said policy makers are ready to implement further stimulus measures if needed as he signaled officials may cut growth forecasts next month. ECB officials were unanimous on more stimulus if needed, Draghi told reporters today.\par \par \uc2 Still, there are fears that Draghi won't actually pull the trigger and that widening d discord among policymakers could hobble the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  at a time of difficulty for the Eurozone economy.\par \par \uc2 Emerging markets, meanwhile, are facing a litany of problems, major among them falling oil prices and geopolitical turmoil.\par \par \uc2 In Brazil, the Ibovespa declined 1.86%. \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in minutes published today that it will remain vigilant regarding inflation after policy makers lifted the target lending rate on Oct. 29 In Mexico, stocks fell 0.11%.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 iShares MSCI Brazil Capped ETF\uc2  ( EWZ) fell 3%, while the \uc2 iShares MSCI Mexico Capped ETF\uc2  ( EWW) fell 0.2%.\par \par \uc2 The ruble, the worse performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the world this year, fell vs the U.S. dollar. Traders are trying to determine how far the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  must drop before \uc2 Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  shores it up with a large \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Micex Index rose 0.15% today. But bigger gains earlier in the trading day were tempered by reports from the Russian state news agency RIA Novosti that Ukraine had begun a large-scale offensive in rebel-held areas in the country's eastern regions, citing Andrei Purgin, deputy premier of the self-proclaimed Donetsk People's Republic.\par \par \uc2 The Market Vectors Russia ETF ( RSX) fell 3.4%. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  More at Barron's Emerging Markets blog,  \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://blogs.barrons.com/emergingmarketsdaily/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://blogs.barrons.com/emergingmarketsdaily/ }}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 November 06, 2014 11:32 ET (16:32 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020141106eab6003n6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw77\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1155\pichgoal600
