\par\par \b \uc2 Russian  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  limits  \highlight22\uc2 forex interventions \highlight\uc2  to $350 mln a day\b0\par\par\uc2 142 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 November 2014\par 08:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Nov 5 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Wednesday it had changed its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy for the rouble exchange rate and was now limiting the size of its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to $350 million a day.\par \par \uc2 In a statement, the bank said the move would significantly increase the flexibility of the exchange rate, meaning the rate will now largely be determined be market factors.\par \par \uc2 The bank also said it would continue to move the rouble's corridor against a dollar-euro basket by five kopecks once the bank has expended $350 million in \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The rouble has lost more than 20 percent of its value against the U.S. dollar this year. (Reporting by Alexander Winning, writing by Jason Bush, editing by Timothy Heritage)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-11-8T07:14:46.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020141105eab5007nc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
