\par\par \b \uc2 Can Russia Right the Ruble? -- Barron's Blog\b0\par\par\uc2 By Johanna Bennett   \par \uc2 529 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 November 2014\par 17:57\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 With the ruble looking like rubbish, \uc2 Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has taken some mighty big steps today.\par \par \uc2 Looking to alleviate speculative pressure as the Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to face heavy selling even after a major rate increase on Friday, \uc2 Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate will be guided mostly by market factors and said it will limit daily \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to $350 million.\par \par \uc2 The ruble plunged to a low on the news, reaching 44.98 per dollar, before recovering a bit to 44.45.\par \par \uc2 As the Wall Street Journal reports:\par \par \uc2 Although Russian officials said they wouldn't burn through reserves to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent more than $30 billion to slow its slide in October. On Friday, the bank announced it was raising interest rates by 1.5 percentage points, bringing its key rate to 9.5%, in an effort to stem the ruble's slide and tame inflation. But the ruble continued to weaken even after the announcement.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the rate hike, along with Wednesday's move to drastically reduce its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slow the ruble's slide, should help steady the market.\par \par \uc2 The ruble has plunged roughly 25% compared to the U.S. dollar this year thanks to sanctions , a stagnating economy and the recent weakening of oil prices.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  shelled out more than $30 billion last month to slow the drop, bring the amount to $70 billion this year. That poses a threat to Russia's reserves which stood at $439.1 billion in late October, down from $510.1 billion at the start of the year.\par \par \uc2 On Friday, policy makers hiked interest rates by 1.5 percentage points to bring the key rate to 9.5%, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to fall.\par \par \uc2 "The problem is that the policy (rate hike) has not prevented the slump in the ruble and has incurred a large cost," wrote Capital Economics analysts Adam Collins and Neil Shearing in a note published earlier this week regarding Friday's interest rate hike.\par \par \uc2 Analysts at Evercore write:\par \par \uc2 USD continues to surge and that should continue to be a headwind for EM generally, but more specifically, commodity based EM. Also, as we highlighted in the Early Thought today, the Ruble has accelerated to the downside as the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced overnight that they would scale down \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  as they are becoming too costly. StreetAccount noted that \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves have declined to the lowest level since 2010 (-70bn this year, but still have 440b). We are not \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  experts at all, but pretty sure countries giving up on \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  as depreciation pressure mounts has been a bad thing in the past.\par \par \uc2 In the ETF arena, The Market Vectors Russia ETF ( RSX) fell 0.33% today. Among other trading vehicles, the Direxion Daily Russia Bear 3X Shares ( RUSS) are up 1.4%, while the Direxion Daily Russia Bull 3X Shares ( RUSL) dropped 1.3%. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  More at Barron's Emerging Markets blog, \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://blogs.barrons.com/emergingmarketsdaily/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://blogs.barrons.com/emergingmarketsdaily/}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 November 05, 2014 11:57 ET (16:57 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020141105eab5003fr\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 Russia Moves Closer To Free Float Exchange Rate\b0\par\par\uc2 256 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 November 2014\par \uc2 RTT News\par \uc2 RTTNEW\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 2014 NoticiasFinancieras. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 (RTTNews) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would reduce \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to further increase the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  flexibility.\par \par \uc2 Accordingly, the bank will limit the volume of \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  to $350 million per day, it said in a statement released Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 It will buy or sell foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the exchange rate of ruble against the U.S. dollar/euro \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket reaches the upper or lower boundary of the band.\par \par \uc2 The bank said it will carry out additional \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if there is any threat to financial stability.\par \par \uc2 The above-mentioned adjustments will increase significantly the ruble exchange rate flexibility and at the same time will drive for a supply and demand balance in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the bank added.\par \par \uc2 This appears to be tantamount to a move towards a fully floating ruble, Neil Shearing, chief emerging markets economist at Capital Economics, said.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to weaken further over the next few days but today's move should help to limit the risk that the recent sharp falls in the ruble develop into a self-fulfilling \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crisis, the economist noted.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Russia raised its key rate by a massive 150 basis points to 9.50 percent last week to counteract the slide in ruble and rising inflation. The rate has been hiked by a cumulative 400 basis points since February.\par \par \uc2 For comments and feedback: contact editorial@rttnews.com\par \par \uc2 Copyright(c) 2014 RTTNews.com. All Rights Reserved\par \par \uc2 Dokument RTTNEW0020141105eab50040i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
