\par\par \b \uc2 Grand Central: Good Morning Ms. Yellen, \uc2 Rand Paul\uc2  on Line One\b0\par\par\uc2 2,037 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 November 2014\par 13:19\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal's Daily Report on Global Central Banks for Wednesday, November 5, 2014:\par \par \uc2 Sign up for the newsletter .\par \par \uc2 Highlights \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    -- Hilsenrath's Take: Good Morning Ms. Yellen, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Rand Paul\f28 \uc2 \f2  on Line One \par  \par  \par    -- \f28 \uc2 \f2 Fed\f28 \uc2 \f2 's Bullard Sees No Need for New Stimulus \par  \par  \par    -- Ultralow Inflation Hits Europe in Different Ways, Complicating Fix \par  \par  \par    -- BOJ Governor Defends "Monetary Bazooka" Approach \par  \par  \par    -- Ruble Sinks to Fresh Lows as \f28 \uc2 \f2 Russian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Scales Back \par       \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 HILSENRATH'S TAKE: GOOD MORNING MS. YELLEN, \f28 \uc2 \f2 RAND PAUL\f28 \uc2 \f2  ON LINE ONE\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Republican victories in Tuesday's election present the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  with new political challenges in Washington.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Republicans wake this morning with at least 52 seats in \f28 \uc2 \f2 the Senate\f28 \uc2 \f2  and 13 additional seats in \f28 \uc2 \f2 the House\f28 \uc2 \f2 . As my colleague Victoria McGrane lays out in a story in today's Wall Street Journal, a GOP-led \f28 \uc2 \f2 Congress\f28 \uc2 \f2  will likely increase scrutiny of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Fed\f28 \uc2 \f2 's interest rate policies as well as its performance as supervisor of the nation's biggest financial institutions.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Richard Shelby, the Alabama Republican who is likely to chair the Senate Banking Committee, supported stripping the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Fed\f28 \uc2 \f2  of its regulatory authority during the Dodd-Frank regulatory debates. Kentucky Republican \f28 \uc2 \f2 Rand Paul\f28 \uc2 \f2  wants to pass legislation subjecting \f28 \uc2 \f2 Fed\f28 \uc2 \f2  interest rate decisions to scrutiny by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Congress\f28 \uc2 \f2 's watchdog, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Government Accountability Office\f28 \uc2 \f2 . \f28 \uc2 \f2 House Financial Services Committee\f28 \uc2 \f2  Chairman Jeb Hensarling has held 11 hearings in the past year scrutinizing the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Fed\f28 \uc2 \f2 's performance and authority. House Republicans have been pressing for a new law requiring the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Fed\f28 \uc2 \f2  to follow a formal rule for setting interest rates akin to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Stanford\f28 \uc2 \f2  Professor John Taylor's "Taylor Rule."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Ms. Yellen has said it would be a "grave mistake" to force the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Fed\f28 \uc2 \f2  to follow an interest rate rule and the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been a fierce opponent of Mr. Paul's "Audit the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Fed\f28 \uc2 \f2 " ambitions.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Another challenge: President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Barack Obama\f28 \uc2 \f2  could now have a hard time filling two empty seats on the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Fed\f28 \uc2 \f2  board, unless he puts up nominees to the Republicans' liking.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Ms. Yellen has already started courting some Republicans. She had Mr. Hensarling in for breakfast in July, in addition to Tennessee Republican Senator \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bob Corker\f28 \uc2 \f2 . She also impressed House Republicans last March in her first testimony before Mr. Hensarling's committee, when she offered to stay as long as they wanted to answer all of their questions. It dragged on for hours and she repeated the effort in \f28 \uc2 \f2 the Senate\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Ms. Yellen has a few things going for her in the coming battles with \f28 \uc2 \f2 Congress\f28 \uc2 \f2 . \f28 \uc2 \f2 The Fed\f28 \uc2 \f2  just ended its bond-buying program and is talking about raising short-term interest rates, which is likely to please Republicans who have opposed the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Fed\f28 \uc2 \f2 's low interest rate policies.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 That could take some pressure off the Fed. Moreover, Republican opposition to low rates could soften now that the party has control of all of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Congress\f28 \uc2 \f2  and has a stake in the faster economic growth that low rates are meant to foster.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Barack Obama\f28 \uc2 \f2 's veto pen stands behind the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Fed\f28 \uc2 \f2 's opposition to ideas like the audit and interest rate rule bills. Ms. Yellen met with Mr. Obama on Monday to discuss the economy.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Ms. Yellen also has presidents of 12 regional \f28 \uc2 \f2 Fed\f28 \uc2 \f2  banks -- big employers in red states like Kansas, Georgia and Texas. They mobilized during the Dodd-Frank debates to press lawmakers in their districts not to strip the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Fed\f28 \uc2 \f2  of its regulatory authorities, and they're close with Ms. Yellen, a former regional bank president herself.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Taken altogether, expect to see a more politically engaged \f28 \uc2 \f2 Fed\f28 \uc2 \f2  at a very sensitive time for policy, and settle in for some very long testimonies by the new Fed Chairwoman to an often hostile audience in \f28 \uc2 \f2 Congress\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Jon Hilsenrath\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MORNING MINUTES: KEY DEVELOPMENTS AROUND THE WORLD\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Fed\f28 \uc2 \f2 's Bullard Sees No Need for New Stimulus--\f28 \uc2 \f2 Fox Business Network\f28 \uc2 \f2 . St. Louis Fed President \f28 \uc2 \f2 James Bullard\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Tuesday he is upbeat about the economy and doesn't see the need for more \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  actions to help keep the economy on track for 3% annual growth. \f28 \uc2 \f2 The Fed\f28 \uc2 \f2 's decision last week to end its bond-buying program was "probably the right judgment for that meeting," Mr. Bullard told \f28 \uc2 \f2 Fox Business Network\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 GOP \f28 \uc2 \f2 Senate\f28 \uc2 \f2  Takeover Likely to Put Fed Under Microscope. Financial executives say a GOP-led \f28 \uc2 \f2 Senate\f28 \uc2 \f2  will likely ratchet up congressional scrutiny of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's interest-rate policies as well as its regulatory duties as overseer of the nation's largest financial firms. Republicans haven't controlled \f28 \uc2 \f2 the Senate\f28 \uc2 \f2  since before the 2008 financial crisis and recession, which put a spotlight on the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Fed\f28 \uc2 \f2  and its powers.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Ultralow Inflation Hits Europe in Different Ways, Complicating Fix. The ultralow inflation becoming entrenched in Europe is playing out in strikingly different ways across the eurozone's 18 economies, complicating attempts to combat it.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Draghi Set To Open at Least One New Chapter in ECB History. When European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mario Draghi\f28 \uc2 \f2  concludes his monthly press conference this week, he will close one chapter in ECB history and get ready for the beginning of a new one. It's just not the chapter many politicians and economists think Draghi should be opening.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EU Cuts Eurozone Growth Forecast. The \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Commission\f28 \uc2 \f2  on Tuesday cut its economic growth forecasts for the eurozone and the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2 , citing the tensions in Ukraine and the Middle East along with a lack of investment. The EU's executive arm also believes inflation in the eurozone will remain below the close-to 2% targeted by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  until at least 2016.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Central Bankers to Challenge Draghi on ECB Leadership Style --Reuters. National \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  heads in the eurozone intend to challenge ECB President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mario Draghi\f28 \uc2 \f2  "over what they see as his secretive management style and erratic communication and will urge him to act more collegially," Reuters reported.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BOJ Governor Defends "Monetary Bazooka" Approach. In his first public speech since the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  surprised markets by taking additional easing measures, Bank of Japan Gov. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Haruhiko Kuroda\f28 \uc2 \f2  stressed the need to do whatever is necessary to annihilate concerns about persistent price falls that have taken root in the country's economy.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Kuroda's Reagan Moment: A "Stay the Course" Plea. In his first public comments since the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2 's controversial big new easing Friday, Gov. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Haruhiko Kuroda\f28 \uc2 \f2  took an unusual detour from his standard economic assessment to nod to -- and try and quell -- rising political opposition to his all-out war on deflation.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Stimulus Gives BOJ Huge New Role in Markets. After firing its latest monetary bazooka, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2  isn't just an influence on financial markets. It is also a huge player in them.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Ruble Sinks to Fresh Lows as \f28 \uc2 \f2 Russian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Scales Back \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Russia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Wednesday it would drastically cut back \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and allow the ruble's exchange rate to be set "primarily by market factors," as the Russian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  continued to face heavy selling pressure even after a major rate increase announced Friday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Iceland's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Cuts Main Interest Rate by 25 Bps to 5.75%. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Iceland's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Wednesday cut its main interest rate for the first time in two years in an effort to boost inflation, which is expected to fall further below its target in the coming months.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thailand's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Keeps Policy Rate Stable at 2.0%. Thailand's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has decided to keep its benchmark interest rate unchanged for the fifth consecutive time as it repeated an assurance that the current rate remains sufficient to help support the country's ongoing economic recovery -- Dow Jones Newswires.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hungarian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Releases Compensation Framework for Loans. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hungary's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Tuesday published the framework that commercial lenders will use when calculating the amount of compensation borrowers will receive for charges made on foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  loans. The methodology was written in cooperation with lenders and experts from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the \f28 \uc2 \f2 National Bank of Hungary\f28 \uc2 \f2  said. It did not release estimates of how much compensation borrowers can expect. --Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 GRAPHIC CONTENT\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 How Low Can the Yen Go? Some investors say they are holding firm on their bearish bets on the yen, anticipating the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's actions will further weaken the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by diminishing the appeal of Japanese debt.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 FORWARD GUIDANCE\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -\f28 \uc2 \f2 Richmond Fed\f28 \uc2 \f2 's Lacker speaks on financial stability in Washington at 8:45 a.m. EST\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -\f28 \uc2 \f2 Minneapolis Fed\f28 \uc2 \f2 's Kocherlakota speaks on the objectives of monetary policy in Virginia, Minn. at 9:15 a.m. EST\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -\f28 \uc2 \f2 Boston Fed\f28 \uc2 \f2 's Rosengren speaks in Lima, Peru at 10 a.m. EST\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -\f28 \uc2 \f2 Poland's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  releases a policy statement\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 RESEARCH\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Exchange Rate Flexibility under the Zero Lower Bound. Would eurozone countries see better economic growth if they had independent \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  with flexible exchange rates? Maybe not, \f28 \uc2 \f2 David Cook\f28 \uc2 \f2  and Michael B. Devereux wrote in a working paper from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dallas Fed\f28 \uc2 \f2 . "When monetary policy is constrained by the zero bound on interest rates, and policy-makers lacks effective forward guidance, then paradoxically, it may be better to have a single \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  than a regime of multiple \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and a flexible exchange rate. Remarkably, this conclusion may still hold even if only a subset of countries in the region are constrained by the zero bound, and the other countries are free to follow optimal monetary policy rules."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 COMMENTARY\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 This is Why the Economy has Fallen and It Can't Get Up. Secular stagnation, Matt O'Brien writes for the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Washington Post\f28 \uc2 \f2 's Wonkblog, means that "the economy can't recover on its own, and if it doesn't soon it might never be able to. We need more inflation, more infrastructure spending, and less tut-tutting about the deficit that, unlike our anemic recovery, isn't an urgent problem. We need to realize that just waiting for catchup growth is the new waiting for Godot--and we can't afford for it to not show up."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 5 Nov 2014 07:19 ET \par Grand Central: Good Morning Ms. Yellen, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Rand Paul\f28 \uc2 \f2  -2-\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The SOMC and Its Core Beliefs. The Shadow Open Market Committee, which was founded in 1973 as an intellectual counter to the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2 , issued a statement of its core beliefs on Monday. Among them: "Monetary policy should be conducted in a rule-like manner and be somewhat countercyclical with respect to output and employment, as long as price stability over the long run is not compromised. We expect the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to announce the policy rule that it follows so that it can be monitored and held accountable."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BASIS POINTS\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - Activity in the eurozone's private sector grew less rapidly in Oct. than initially estimated, while weak flows of new orders suggest the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  area's economy will remain trapped in a period of low or no growth for some months to come.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - Indonesia's economy grew at its slowest pace in five years in the third quarter and the outlook is dim for a turnaround soon, throwing a challenge to the new president.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - \f28 \uc2 \f2 Romania's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Tuesday lowered its policy rate to 2.75% from 3%, citing persistently low inflation.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - The ECB on Tuesday officially took over supervision of the eurozone's banks.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - The U.S. trade gap widened in September as exports posted the largest drop since February, a sign of weaker demand for American-made goods that could underscore concerns about a global growth slowdown.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SIGN UP: Grand Central, straight to your inbox.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 FEEDBACK LOOP: Send us your tips, suggestions and feedback. Write to: Jon.Hilsenrath@wsj.com; Victoria.McGrane@wsj.com; Pedro.daCosta@wsj.com; Michael.Derby@wsj.com; Nell.Henderson@wsj.com; Brian.Blackstone@wsj.com; jason.douglas@wsj.com; Ben.Leubsdorf@wsj.com; Paul.Hannon@wsj.com; Jacob.Schlesinger@wsj.com sarah.portlock@wsj.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Follow us on \f28 \uc2 \f2 Twitter\f28 \uc2 \f2 : @WSJCentralBanks, @NHendersonWSJ, @pdacosta, @Blackstonebrian, @PaulHannon29, @michaelsderby, @vgmac, @wsj_douglasj, @BenLeubsdorf, @JMSchels, @MargitFeher @NirmalaMenon @ToddBuell @sarahportlock \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 November 05, 2014 07:19 ET (12:19 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020141105eab50023y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
