\par\par \b \uc2 Ruble Still Priced Above its Fair Value -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,629 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 November 2014\par 12:43\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 1143 GMT \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  sees the fair value of the ruble under "full sanctions, no roll-overs and oil around $85/barrel" at around 53 versus the bi-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket, compared to 49.15 currently. Given the extreme assumptions Goldman sees a possibility of a strengthening of the ruble in the short run. Doesn't expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily to support the ruble at levels which are impossible to defend in the long run. Says the banking system will be able to withstand the slide. USD/RUB is currently at 44.23.(alexander.kolyandr@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 1128 GMT The South Africa Chamber of Commerce and Industry says factory and mine managers aren't sure government officials have the willpower to adopt policies that would reverse years of weak growth, driving business confidence to a 15-year low. "The challenge to improving business confidence is for the private sector to be convinced that the economy is entering a new era of economic growth," the chamber wrote in a statement. That isn't happening. South Africa was surpassed in April by Nigeria as Africa's largest economy, and the finance ministry expects economic growth to reach just 1.4% this year. (patrick.mcgroarty@wsj.com). \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0000 GMT (\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 )--The range floor at 129.50 on the December BTP future remains elusive, following the bounce from the current session low at 129.70. That said, bulls need to ram home their advantage by forcing a break above projected resistance at 130.29, and a push into new session highs above 130.27 should achieve this, opening Tuesday's lower high at 130.51 and Monday's peak at 130.78. Bears would only regain control on a break below 120.70, exposing 129.50 and threatening additional downside risk to 128.94. The December BTP future is at 130.06.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Francis Bray, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones Chief Technical\f28 \uc2 \f2  Analyst For Europe.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (francis.bray@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security or \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 . The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1121 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--Wouter Sturkenboom, senior investment strategist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Russell Investments\f28 \uc2 \f2 , doesn't expect the ECB to extend its asset purchase program to corporate bonds any time soon. "The focus of tomorrow's ECB meeting will be on the start of its purchases of asset backed securities and covered bonds and what we imagine will be a firm denunciation of the rumours surrounding plans to buy corporate debt," he writes in a note. "Of course, such a denunciation will be sugar coated by [Mario] Draghi by referring to the willingness of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Governing Council\f28 \uc2 \f2  to do more if needed," he adds. (josie.cox@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1112 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--Ireland's unemployment rate continued to edge down in October, dropping by the now customary tenth of a percentage point to 11.0% from 11.1%. Seasonally adjusted, 3,500 people came off the unemployment register, bringing the total for the 12 months to 37,882. The jobless rate peaked at 15.1% in Feb. 2012, and has been falling pretty steadily since then. But it remains very high, and flattered by large outflows of migrants in the years since the financial crisis broke in 2008. So while the economy is forecast by the EU to be the fastest growing in Europe this year and next, the real test of recovery will be whether the jobless decline accelerates in coming months. (paul.hannon@wsj.com. Twitter: @PaulHannon29) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1102 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Swiss National Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  may have to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to weaken the Swiss franc which has continued to strengthen against the euro, says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commerzbank\f28 \uc2 \f2 . There has been continuous downward trend in EUR/CHF since February, which many would have thought unlikely in view of the SNB's CHF1.20 per euro floor, the bank notes. Today's Swiss inflation figures, which came in at 0%, are unlikely to please the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . "As EUR-CHF eased back as far as 1.2033 this morning the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  pair is rapidly approaching levels at which SNB \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  might become necessary again," says analyst Esther Maria Reichelt. EUR-CHF trading at 1.2041. (john.revill@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1037 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--GBP/USD continues to slide after the weak October UK services PMI print and racks up a fresh 2014 low of 1.5870. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Barclays\f28 \uc2 \f2  says breach of the previous year-to-date low around 1.5875 opens the downside to 1.5850, and then the 1.5750-1.5720 area. gary.stride@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1019 GMT \f28 \uc2 \f2 Russell Investments\f28 \uc2 \f2  expect a "firm denunciation of the rumors surrounding plans to buy corporate debt" at the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's meeting Thursday, says Wouter Sturkenboom, senior investment strategist for EMEA. "Of course, such a denunciation will be sugar coated by [ECB president Mario] Draghi by referring to the willingness of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Governing Council\f28 \uc2 \f2  to do more if needed. On inflation, Mr. Sturkenboom expects Mr. Draghi to underline the impact of a lower euro and energy prices, while acknowledging the risk of declining medium-term inflation expectations, while on growth he is expected to repeat the need for fiscal and monetary policy to reinforce each other. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Russell Investments\f28 \uc2 \f2  has $260 billion assets under management as of end-September. (emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1004 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--After spending around $30 billion to slow the ruble's drop in October, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Russia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has scaled down \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to a maximum of $350 million per day, and this should limit risks that the ruble's weakness develops into a self-fulfilling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  crisis, says Capital Economics. It expects the ruble to weaken further over the coming days, but adds the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could, "find a floor more quickly than would have been the case under the old framework." Apart from fundamental factors and geopolitical risks, the ruble has tended to suffer from speculative bets when the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  carries out steady, predictable \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Concerns that the ruble could depreciate sharply once the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  lets it float freely next year also added to the downside pressure. "Today's move helps to mitigate this threat," says Capital Economics, seeing the ruble at around 45 per dollar over the next six months. (andrey.ostroukh@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1003 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--Czech retail sales data smashed expectations but won't be enought to alter the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's easy monetary policy, says Radomir Jac, chief analyst at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Generali\f28 \uc2 \f2  PPF Asset Management, as it's the external (ie eurozone) environment which dominates policy-setters' thoughts. Sales soared 6.2%, but Mr. Jac doubts that this pace will be sustainable. The headline interest rate is expected to stay put at its 0.05% record low Thursday. (leos.rousek@wsj.com, @LeoRousek) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1002 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--Eurozone retail services fell 1.3% in September from August, the largest month-to-month decline since April 2012, and a larger drop than the 1.0% forecast by economists. The August increase was revised down to 0.9% from 1.2%, so with sales also having fallen in July, it looks like a weak quarter. The headline number was bad enough, but what may really worry policy makers is the 2.2% drop recorded in non-food sales, excluding automotive fuels. That's the largest month-to-month decline since September 1999 in a category that includes the kinds of things you might postpone purchases of if you thought prices were going to fall. Which is the kind of behavior that leads to deflation. (paul.hannon@wsj.com; Twitter: @PaulHannon29) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0959 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Thailand's military junta leader and Prime Minister General Prayuth Chan-ocha turns down suggestions that martial law will soon be lifted. "I never spoke about that. No one has ever asked me about this, not even foreign [governments]," Prayuth says. Thailand's travel industry, which contributes around 10% to gross domestic product, has been hoping for an end to martial law--imposed a few days before the military coup on May 22--at least in some major tourist destinations to revive business. According to the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Thailand\f28 \uc2 \f2 , as of September, the number of foreign tourists remained below its normal trend as "many countries still maintained their travel warning advisory levels." Official data show tourist arrivals fell 10.1% on-year though the number rose 4.1% on-quarter in the third quarter. (nopparat.chaichalearmmongkol@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 November 05, 2014 06:43 ET (11:43 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020141105eab50020g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
