\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Russia \highlight\uc2  Scales Back  \highlight22\uc2 FX Intervention \highlight\uc2 , Ruble Slides -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,606 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 November 2014\par 09:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0805 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ]--\b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Wednesday it had scaled down its \b \highlight22\uc2 FX interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to a daily maximum of $350 million. "Thus the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has de facto let the ruble float freely," says Pavel Demeshchik, a dealer at \uc2 ING\uc2 . The ruble headed to fresh record lows after the announcement. The dollar hit RUB44.98, a move exacerbated by falling oil prices. Though the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  claims reduced \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  will make it harder to bet on the ruble weakening, Mr. Demeshchik says the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to fall further in a "thin and jittery" market unless oil prices recover above $90 per barrel. (andrey.ostroukh@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 0801 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ]--The \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  survey forecast for the dominant U.K. services sector PMI is for 58.5, a small slip from the 58.7 seen in September. U.K. PMI data has been mixed in October, with Tuesday's U.K. construction reading sharply disappointing at a 5-month low 61.4 vs 64.2 last, while Monday's manufacturing PMI surprised to the upside at 53.2 vs 51.5 in September. GBP/USD now at 1.5965. (gary.stride@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0757 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--USD/JPY printed a fresh 7-year high, and EUR/JPY a 7-month high, after BoJ Governor Kuroda took a leaf out of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mario Draghi\f28 \uc2 \f2 's book, saying there were no limits to steps the bank would take to defeat deflation. Elsewhere tumbling oil prices hurt RUB and CAD, the former falling to fresh record lows vs USD while the Loonie is at its weakest in 5 years against the greenback. Up ahead service PMIs and \f28 \uc2 \f2 ADP\f28 \uc2 \f2  employment survey grab attention. (gary.stride@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0755 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Indonesia's economy continues a steady decline, dropping to its lowest pace of growth in five years in the third quarter, but "going forward, the slide should be controlled," OCBC economist Wellian Wiranto tells The Wall Street Journal. "Fourth quarter print might still be a rather low one, especially if the government finds the guts to do a chunky fuel price increase," he says. He adds that 2015 should turn rosier as investment sentiment improves after a long political season and fiscal spending on infrastructure starts to kick in. For a new president, "the good thing is the numbers provide a low base for him," he adds. (ben.otto@wsj.com; \f28 \uc2 \f2 Twitter\f28 \uc2 \f2 : @benottoWSJ) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0749 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] On Wednesday, a group of 20 Philippine and foreign business groups teamed up in Manila to accuse the country's Bureau of Internal Revenue of withholding around $330 million in value added tax refunds. While the bureau has committed to processing new claims within 120 days, older cases are being left to the courts, meaning companies face years of legal delays in recovering their money, the groups' representative complained. "We feel business is being short-changed. It's so unfair," said Henry Schumacher, vice president for external affairs at the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Chamber of Commerce\f28 \uc2 \f2 , one of the 20 groups. However, BIR Commissioner \f28 \uc2 \f2 Kim Jacinto-Henares\f28 \uc2 \f2  denied she was deliberately withholding repayments, and suggested the business groups had greatly overestimated the amount of reclaimable VAT. "If they feel their rights have been trampled upon, the code says they should go to the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Court of Tax Appeals\f28 \uc2 \f2 ," she said. (trefor.moss@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0744 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] China's labor market remains resilient despite slowing economic growth as the country has passed a key turning point in its labor market, Nomura economists say. The ratio between the number of vacancies and the number of job seekers edged down to 1.09 in the third quarter, meaning there are 109 job vacancies for every 100 job seekers, a tad down from 1.11 in the second quarter, a recent government survey shows. "The data reinforces our view that China has passed the Lewis turning point and that potential growth is slowing, probably to around 7% this year," they say in a note to clients. The Lewis Turning Point, named after Nobel laureate Arthur Lewis, is the point when labor becomes scarce enough that wages rise sharply, industrial profits are squeezed and investment falls. The Chinese economy grew 7.3% on year in the second quarter, down from 7.5% in the second. (liyan.qi@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0740 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Venezuela's Amuay refinery suffered its latest interruption of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Tuesday night when a power outage temporarily knocked the facility offline. Authorities hinted at suspicious causes for the blackout, but government detractors are sure to renew accusations that a lack of investment in the sector has led to declining output and a shrinking number of cash-generating oil exports. The oil-rich country has earmarked more than a third of its slipping production to repay creditors and provide regional allies with deeply discounted oil. With oil prices entering a possibly extended slump, Venezuela will be pressured to dust off long-ignored plans to increase productivity. (Ezequiel.minaya@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0730 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Indonesia posted its lowest growth rate in five years--5% on-year in the third quarter--and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Credit Suisse\f28 \uc2 \f2  says recovery isn't happening anytime soon. "A number of negative factors [are] capping growth over the next six months," \f28 \uc2 \f2 Credit Suisse\f28 \uc2 \f2  economist Santitarn Sathirathai writes in a research note, pointing to likely higher fuel prices sapping private consumption and investment, plus continued weak prices for some of the country's most important commodity exports like coal. That means growth could dip below 5% in the next two quarters, he says--it averaged 6.2% in 2011-2013. But in the long run domestic demand will pick up--if President Joko Widodo delivers on redirecting wasteful fuel subsidies and removing blocks to foreign investment. (ben.otto@wsj.com; @benottoWSJ) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0720 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The Philippine government remains committed to reforming the country's tax code in response to persistent complaints that the system is too complicated, according to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Kim Jacinto-Henares\f28 \uc2 \f2 , the Commissioner of the Bureau of Internal Revenue. "A bill will be introduced in mid-2015," says Jacinto-Henares. "We've agreed to do a comprehensive tax reform, to simplify it to improve the bracketing of the rates, and remove some of the exemptions." She said that a simpler code would help companies and individuals to pay the right amount of tax, but warned that there was still a lasting culture of tax-avoidance in the country. "But I don't think it's just a problem of non-compliance with tax law," she said. "If you look at the Philippines, there's a problem with compliance with the law, period." (trefor.moss@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0649 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Democrat David Ige won Hawaii's gubernatorial election Tuesday night, according to projections by the Associated Press, ensuring the top statewide office remained in his party's hands despite a contentious primary earlier this year that saw him beating the incumbent in a historic upset. The win for Ige, 57, an engineer, longtime legislator and chair of the state senate's committee on ways and means, came after he defeated the incumbent governor, Neil Abercrombie. It was the first time since Hawaiian statehood in 1959 that an incumbent governor had lost a primary challenge. (alejandro.lazo@wsj.com; \f28 \uc2 \f2 Twitter\f28 \uc2 \f2 : @AlejandroLazo) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0647 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Republican Charlie Baker defeated Democrat state Attorney General \f28 \uc2 \f2 Martha Coakley\f28 \uc2 \f2  in Tuesday's election to become the next governor of Massachusetts. Baker, a former health care chief executive who served in two prior Republican governors' cabinets, campaigned on cleaning up the management of state government following scandals in the state's child-welfare and criminal-justice systems. He appealed to many independent voters tired of Democrat control of state government, according to polls. Baker made implementing welfare reform a priority. He also said he wants to expand the number of charter schools in the state to improve early-childhood education, and to reduce the costs of college education. (kris.maher@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0612 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] USD/Asia rallies broadly after a dovish tone in a Wednesday speech by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2 's governor gave USD/JPY a fresh boost. BOJ chief \f28 \uc2 \f2 Haruhiko Kuroda\f28 \uc2 \f2  reiterated that he will do whatever it takes to achieve the 2.0% inflation target, standing firmly behind the surprise decision to expand the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's asset purchase program last Friday. As USD/JPY hit a new seven-year high, USD/KRW and USD/MYR rallied to nine-month peaks, while USD/SGD rose to a level not seen since May 2012. The yen's sharp depreciation in recent days has been a trigger for proxy bets in other Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Most sensitive to changes in the yen's value is the South Korea won due to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Korea\f28 \uc2 \f2 's preference for a favorable JPY/KRW exchange rate that improves export competitiveness. Singapore's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has the yen as a component of its trade-weighted \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  exchange basket model--used to determine the fair value for the Singapore dollar. (ewen.chew@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 November 05, 2014 03:05 ET (08:05 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020141105eab5001c4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
