\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Rouble still slumping after big Russian rate hike\b0\par\par\uc2 532 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Oktober 2014\par 14:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 (Updates to reflect trading after c.bank meeting)\par \par \uc2 By Alexander Winning and Vladimir Abramov\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Oct 31 (Reuters) - The rouble slumped around 3 percent against the dollar on Friday, giving back almost all its sharp gains of the previous session, even after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hiked its key interest rate by more than the market had expected.\par \par \uc2 At 1350 GMT, the rouble was 3.09 percent weaker against the dollar at 42.93 and lost 2.52 percent to trade at 53.74 versus the euro.\par \par \uc2 That left the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  2.8 percent weaker at 47.79 against the dollar-euro basket used by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to gauge the rouble's nominal exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 The rouble was briefly buoyed by the 150 basis point rate hike but resumed its fall after the bank said it had not altered its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy.\par \par \uc2 There had been speculation the bank might use Friday's meeting to scrap the rouble's trading band ahead of schedule or tweak policy to enable bigger \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Coupled with talk of a large, one-off \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the bank and a possible deal between \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Ukraine over Crimea, such speculation had helped the rouble close up over 3 percent on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 "My concern is that the pressure on the rouble that we saw before this (rate meeting) was hardly the result of interest rates being too low," said VTB Capital economist Vladimir Kolychev.\par \par \uc2 "I very much want to believe that this (rate rise) will help the rouble. If not, then the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will have to change its exchange rate policy."\par \par \uc2 The rouble has lost around 20 percent of its value against the dollar this year. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been weakened by falling oil prices, risk aversion towards Russia because of its role in the Ukraine conflict, and demand for foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from Russian companies shut out of Western capital markets.\par \par \uc2 Applying further downwards pressure on Friday, the dollar strengthened against a basket of major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while Brent crude fell more than a dollar to below $85 a barrel.\par \par \uc2 Oil is one of Russia's chief exports, and sales of oil and gas account for up to half of federal budget revenues.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily to defend the rouble this month, spending at least $25 billion in reserves. Since the start of the year it has spent around $70 billion propping up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Analysts polled by Reuters this week had predicted the bank would raise its key lending rate by 50 bps on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Russian stock indexes were mixed. The dollar-denominated RTS index was down 1.1 percent at 1,086 points, dragged down by the weaker rouble.\par \par \uc2 In contrast the rouble-based MICEX rose 1.8 percent to 1,479 points, helped by a deal reached late on Thursday between Russia and Ukraine over winter gas supplies.\par \par \uc2 For rouble poll data see\par \par \uc2 For Russian equities guide see\par \par \uc2 For Russian treasury bonds see\par \par \uc2 Russia in graphics: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/dun63s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/dun63s}}}\uc2  (Additional reporting by Jason Bush, Oksana Kobzeva and Polina Devitt; Editing by Catherine Evans) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-10-31T14:53:45.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020141031eaav007e1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
