\par\par \b \uc2 Standard Bank Flips To EUR/USD Seller -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,480 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Oktober 2014\par 12:36\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 1136 GMT After adopting a neutral stance on EUR/USD just yesterday, \uc2 Standard Bank\uc2 's trading model has turned bearish on the rate. The bank subsequently sells at the current level of 1.2570, targeting 1.2270 with a 1.2780 stop-loss. (gary.stride@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 1132 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ]--The Bank of Russia's 1.5 percentage point rate hike is only justifiable as at attempt to stem ruble weakness and is unlikely to succeed, according to Dmitri Petrov of Nomura. He says the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is falling on geopolitics and a liquidity shortage, and that it would take further changes in Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy to stop it. He calls the move 'over tightening' from an inflation-fighting perspective. alexander.kolyandr@wsj.com \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 7:30 EDT - We said at the start of the month that October could be treacherous for stocks. We had no idea, though, just how volatile things would be. But in the end it's of no matter to bulls as the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow\f28 \uc2 \f2  industrials is set to see its 8th gain for the month in the past 10 years between yesterday's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Visa\f28 \uc2 \f2  (V)-fueled jump and today's party courtesy of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2  helping put the early-month pullback further in the rear view. Amid stocks' surge (S&P 500 futures are up 21 after earlier rising as much as 28), investors are selling oil and gold. They're off 1% and 2%, respectively as the dollar is up nearly 2.5 yen at around Y111.75. Treasurys are lower, putting the 10-year yield at 2.33%. (kevin.kingsbury@wsj.com; @kevinkingsbury)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1129 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--Eurozone banks will repay EUR3.9 billion in three-year ECB loans next week, the ECB said in its weekly update. That's down from EUR5.7 billion that were repaid this week. Still, the figures highlight the challenge the ECB faces as it aims to significantly increase the size of its balance sheet. New four-year loans as well as covered bond and ABS purchases will help in that respect, but the balance sheet will also be reduced by repayments of three-year loans under the previous lending program. (brian.blackstone@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0000 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The strong bounce from the session low at 126-065 on the December \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  Note future targets the near-term range high at 126-245 on the 60-minute chart. Resistance at 126-190 blocks the upward path to Thursday's 126-245 high, although with former range lows at 126-260 reverting to resistance, it would take a concerted wave of bull pressure to force a break higher. The prize for success would be the completion of a double-bottom base at the 126-060/126-065 recent lows on the 60-minute chart, creating additional upside scope to 127-110. Failure to hold onto support at 126-060/126-065 would extend the broader bear wave from the October 15 peak at 130-170, exposing 125-195. The December \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  Note future is at 126-115.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Francis Bray, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones Chief Technical\f28 \uc2 \f2  Analyst For Europe.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (francis.bray@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security or \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 . The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1125 GMT For the first time in months Russia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  mentions a possibility of a future monetary easing in the statement accompanying today's base rate hike of 150 basis points. "Should the external conditions improve, and inflation expectations show a stable downward trend, the Bank of Russia will be ready to start monetary policy easing," the Bank of Russia says. In markets, the Micex index is 1.3% higher at 1471.23 and the ruble has eased to 42.20 against the U.S. dollar, following its rally earlier. (alexander.kolyandr@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1119 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--From a technical viewpoint, USD/JPY has just reached a 50% retracement of the entire move down from the 1998 peak of 147.62. Longs taking some profit would not be a great surprise says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commerzbank\f28 \uc2 \f2  technical analyst \f28 \uc2 \f2 Karen Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 , however she adds that this level (111.47) is seen a break-point for an eventual move to 120.00. Now at 111.65. gary.stride@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1107 GMT Turkey's September trade deficit narrows due to robust export growth, supported by the recovery of trade with the Middle East, says Finansbank. Turkey's trade deficit narrowed to $6.93 billion in September from $7.6 billion a year earlier. "Adverse effects of geopolitical developments on Turkey's exports seem to have faded," says Finansbank. Exports to Iraq decreased by 11% on the year in September, as opposed to decreases by 45% in July and 26% in August. It notes that data suggest the country's trade deficit will continue to decline in the remainder of this year. (yeliz.candemir@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 07:04 EDT - \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2  is working to ensure the global liquidity taps remain wide open. Bank's decision to boost its asset purchase program caught markets off-guard. Whether additional quantitative easing can revive the flagging Abenomics program is an open question. But it gave global equity markets another shot in the arm after positive U.S. GDP data fuelled Wall Street's rally Thursday. The next question is what it does to exacerbate increasing misalignments in world exchange rates. The dollar will further gain against the yen and any others that will be inclined to respond to Japan's move by talking or actively pushing their own \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  down. That exchange rate misalignment only makes it harder for countries whose financial woes are forcing their central banks' to hike interest rates against their wishes and to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to increase, rather than weaken their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  -- \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Russia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which hiked rate today, being the best case in point. (michael.casey@wsj.com and alen.mattich@wsj.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1058 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--Greece's consumer confidence index grew for the third quarter in a row in the June-September period of 2014, Nielsen figures showed. The index rose to 56 points in the third quarter as Greeks became less pessimistic over their finances and their ability to spend. But, more Greeks, compared with the second quarter, believe that the country was in recession and that it will remain on a negative trend for at least next year. Labor security remained their biggest concern, rising by 5% to 47%. (nektaria.stamouli@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1057 GMT Greek retail sales rose by 7.4% in August on year by volume, data from the national statistics agency showed, after a downwardly revised 4.7% increase in July. Sales volumes rose for the third straight month, showing a boost in consumer spending during the third quarter of 2014. On a monthly basis the volume of retail trade recorded a 6.6% rise. The turnover index in retail trade recorded an increase of 4.5% in August on year and a 3.3% increase on a monthly basis. (nektaria.stamouli@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 6:55 EDT - US inflation has been subdued for a while now. But there might be another factor at work when Commerce releases the September PCE reading at 8:30. Seasonally adjusted core inflation, as measured by both the PCE and \f28 \uc2 \f2 CPI\f28 \uc2 \f2  gauges, tends to run higher in 1H than 2H, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Fed\f28 \uc2 \f2  economist Ekaterina Peneva pointed out earlier this month in a post on the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Fed\f28 \uc2 \f2 's website. "The potential presence of residual seasonality in the core inflation data suggest that awareness of this pattern may be useful for anyone trying to interpret or understand current inflation developments." (ben.leubsdorf@wsj.com; @BenLeubsdorf)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 October 31, 2014 07:36 ET (11:36 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020141031eaav001xi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
