\par\par \b \uc2 *Russia's Putin Reiterates Commitment to Move to Floating Exchange Rate\b0\par\par\uc2 239 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Oktober 2014\par 16:31\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 24 Oct 2014 10:31 ET *\b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Putin: \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Will \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to Smooth \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Moves\par \par \uc2 24 Oct 2014 10:36 ET *Russia's Putin: 'We Will Not Burn Up Our Reserves Thoughtlessly'\par \par \uc2 24 Oct 2014 11:26 ET  Russia's Putin Reiterates Commitment to Free Floating \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par   By Andrey Ostroukh \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MOSCOW--Russian President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Vladimir Putin\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Friday the country won't "burn up reserves thoughtlessly" as he reiterated his commitment to a free- floating \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Russia is planning to switch to an inflation targeting policy next year, abandoning its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategy which has helped steer the ruble exchange rate through some difficult times lately.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Speaking at an annual meeting of the Valdai discussion club, held in Sochi, Mr. Putin said that Russia would gradually switch to the ruble's free float.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 He added that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves will be used for a "particular balancing" of the exchange rate, reiterating the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's long-term commitment.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Russia's gold-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves stood at $443.8 billion in mid-October, far below a peak of nearly $600 billion seen before the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  spent one third of reserves to limit the ruble's depreciation during the crisis of 2008-2009.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Andrey Ostroukh at andrey.ostroukh@wsj.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 October 24, 2014 11:26 ET (15:26 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020141024eaao001wu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
