\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Russian assets slide ahead of \uc2 S&P\uc2  rating review\b0\par\par\uc2 559 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Oktober 2014\par 12:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 (Adds comments, details throughout)\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Oct 24 (Reuters) - Russian assets slid on Friday before a ratings review by \uc2 Standard and Poor's\uc2 , which might downgrade Russia's debt to 'junk' status, and a weekend parliamentary election in Ukraine that could enflame East-West tensions.\par \par \uc2 The rouble was badly hit. It has already been bruised by strong demand for dollars from Russian companies shut out of international capital markets by Western sanctions over Ukraine, and is down 22 percent since the start of the year, its worst since 1998.\par \par \uc2 By 1015 GMT, it was 0.64 percent weaker against the dollar at 41.97. It also had lost 0.53 percent to trade at 53.08 versus the euro after earlier hitting new lows against both \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  once more to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with traders saying the bank has now spent close to $17 billion so far this month in market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "A continuation of the negative mood on foreign markets, as well as the risk of a downgrade of Russia's sovereign rating, are forcing market participants to hurry to get rid of their roubles," analysts at \uc2 Bank Zenit\uc2  said in a note.\par \par \uc2 The rouble was 0.6 percent weaker at 46.98 against the dollar-euro basket the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  uses to gauge the rouble's nominal exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said early on Friday it had shifted the rouble's trading band by 40 kopecks a day before, to 37.70 to 46.70 against the basket - the largest daily shift in the rouble's trading band so far this year. Once the rouble reaches the band's limits, the bank automatically conducts market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Analysts said they do not think \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's macroeconomic fundamentals warrant a downgrade and \uc2 S&P\uc2  is unlikely to impose one. But lingering political tensions around Ukraine and a dramatic collapse in prices for oil, one of Russia's chief exports, have fuelled market fears.\par \par \uc2 S&P\uc2  is expected to announce its verdict after the market closes. Its rating is already BBB-, just a step away from non-investment status, and carries a 'negative outlook', meaning there is at least a one-in-three chance of a downgrade at some point over the next two years.\par \par \uc2 Russian shares also fell on Friday, hurt by the same broad-based risk aversion linked to the \uc2 S&P\uc2  decision and the decline in oil prices.\par \par \uc2 Brent crude fell to $86 a barrel after a confirmed case of Ebola in New York raised fears of travel restrictions that could weaken jet fuel demand, and poor economic growth outlooks weighed on projected oil consumption.\par \par \uc2 The dollar-denominated RTS index was down 0.9 percent at 1,026 points, 10 points away from its low for the year. The rouble-based MICEX was 0.3 percent lower at 1,368 points. Top bank \uc2 Sberbank\uc2  was 0.5 percent lower, while oil producer Rosneft was down 0.3 percent.\par \par \uc2 For rouble poll data see\par \par \uc2 For Russian equities guide see\par \par \uc2 For Russian treasury bonds see\par \par \uc2 Russia in graphics: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/dun63s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/dun63s}}}\uc2  (Reporting by Alexander Winning and Lidia Kelly in Moscow and Marc Jones in London; Editing by Jason Bush, Larry King) \par \par \uc2 