\par\par \b \uc2 *Ruble Weakens to All-Time Low of RUB46.8 per Euro-Dollar Basket\b0\par\par\uc2 327 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Oktober 2014\par 08:08\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Corrections and Amplifications\par \par \uc2 This headline was corrected at 06:17 GMT. The original misstated the price of the ruble as RUB47.\par \par \uc2 24 Oct 2014 02:08 ET *Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  Says Didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to Support Ruble Oct 22\par \par \uc2 24 Oct 2014 02:09 ET *Bank of Russia Shifted Ruble Band to RUB37.7-46.7 per Basket Oct 23\par \par \uc2 24 Oct 2014 02:15 ET *CORRECT: Ruble Weakens to Low of RUB46.8, Not RUB47, per Euro-Dollar Basket\par \par \uc2 24 Oct 2014 02:47 ET  Ruble Falls Amid Credit-Rating Concerns\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par By Andrey Ostroukh \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MOSCOW--The Russian ruble slid to yet another all-time low against the euro-dollar basket of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as investors wait for the latest report on the country's creditworthiness from \f28 \uc2 \f2 Standard & Poor's\f28 \uc2 \f2  Inc., expected later Friday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 S&P\f28 \uc2 \f2  has Russia's low investment-grade credit rating on negative watch.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Any downgrade would make the country's government bonds non investment grade, otherwise known as "junk".\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The ruble, battered this month by sliding oil prices, had eased 0.2% to its weakest ever level of 46.8 against the euro-dollar basket in the first minutes of trade on the Moscow exchange.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which uses the basket to track the domestic \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market, said Friday it shifted the ruble's trading band to 37.70-46.70 closer to the end of the main trading session on Thursday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The ruble's trading levels now suggest that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has moved the band 48 times so far this month, shifting it by 5 kopecks each time after selling $350 million on the lower end of the corridor, according to the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rule. This takes \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  spent on supporting the plummeting ruble to as much as $16.8 billion since early October.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 October 24, 2014 02:47 ET (06:47 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020141024eaao000zu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
