\par\par \b \uc2 Bank of  \highlight22\uc2 Russia \highlight\uc2  Didn't  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2  in Market on Oct 20 For First Time This Month\b0\par\par\uc2 By Andrey Ostroukh\u8236\'20\'2C   \par \uc2 244 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Oktober 2014\par 08:59\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW--Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Wednesday it didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  the market to support the ruble on Oct. 20, spending no funds from its reserves for the first time since the beginning of the month.\par \par \uc2 The ruble, which has fallen around 20% against the dollar so far this year, recovered slightly this week thanks to domestic tax payments, which prompt export-focused companies to convert their dollar and euro revenues to meet local liabilities.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, the ruble didn't touch the weak end of its floating band, which kept the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  after it spent as much as $13.3 billion from \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves since early October.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  keeps the ruble within a floating band and starts selling dollars and euros to cushion the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decline whenever the ruble moves to the weak boundary of the band. After selling $350 million, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  shifts the ruble's trading band higher by 5 kopecks.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also said Wednesday it didn't move the ruble's band on Oct. 21, keeping it at 37.30-46.30 versus the euro-dollar basket. The ruble was steady in early trade at 45.96 against the basket.\par \par \uc2 Write to Andrey Ostroukh at andrey.ostroukh@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 October 22, 2014 02:59 ET (06:59 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020141022eaam000kk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
