\par\par \b \uc2 Bank Of  \highlight22\uc2 Russia \highlight\uc2  Refrains From  \highlight22\uc2 Intervening \highlight\uc2  Thanks To Tax Duties -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,421 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Oktober 2014\par 10:19\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0819 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ]--Russia's monthly taxes, paid at the end of every month, help the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to refrain from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  and save \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves. Export-focused companies usually convert their dollar and euro revenues into rubles to meet local tax duties in the second half of every month. "We think that the ruble's depreciation will be limited by tax payments and steady oil prices until the Bank of Russia rate meeting," Rosbank says. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has spent more than $13 billion to prop up the ruble so far this month, will next meet on rates on Oct 31. The ruble trades at 46.18 versus the euro-dollar basket, away from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level of 46.30 per basket. (andrey.ostroukh@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 0800 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] Overnight data showed that China gross domestic product growth slowed, but at 7.3% year-on-year in the third quarter this was less than expected, says \uc2 Barclays\uc2 . "We still expect ongoing support for growth from the government's 'targeted easing' measures, a relaxation of macroprudential measures to support the property market, and new investment projects," \uc2 Barclays\uc2  strategists say. Nonetheless, they expect the government to set a lower GDP growth target of 7% for 2015 from 7.5% in 2014. The bank has a below-consensus 2015 forecast of 6.9%. (chiara.albanese@wsj.com; \uc2 Twitter\uc2 : @chiaraalbanese) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0759 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--The 2.75% July 2028 bond, of which Finland will sell up to EUR1 billion Tuesday, has underperformed Dutch and Austrian peers, SocGen notes. The auction itself explains some of this, the French bank says, but not all, as tensions between Russia and the West over Ukraine are also weighing on Finnish debt. As it doesn't expect swift resolution here, SocGen is cautious about the auction. (emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0752 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--When the German bank took a snapshot of its EUR/USD order book earlier Tuesday, the rate was trading at 1.2816 and there were more sell than buy orders. Things stayed that way until around 1.2740, where the sell and buy densities were about equal, suggesting that a downmove would lose steam in this area. EUR/USD just printed a fresh day high of 1.2840. gary.stride@dowjones.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0741 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] China's better than expected growth in the third quarter, which came out at 7.3% year-on-year, gave little cheer to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Morgan Stanley\f28 \uc2 \f2  with the bank pointing out that growth in domestic demand is still soft. The bank expects Beijing to implement more easing, which could take the form of reduced funding costs, while at same time supporting the ailing property market and infrastructure spending. (Daniel.Inman@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0717 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--\f28 \uc2 \f2 Danske Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  recommends investors buy Norway's 3% March 2024 government bond at Tuesday's auction, either against Bunds or asset-swapped. The bond is broadly expected to be reopened a few more times--which may cause price pressure via more issuance, but, given "the chronic demand" for level-1 assets for liquidity portfolios among Norwegian banks, the bond is expected to become more expensive in the times ahead. The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Norges Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  will auction NOK3 billion, with results shortly after 0900 GMT. (emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ("USD Retreats As U.S. Yields Fall, \f28 \uc2 \f2 China Data\f28 \uc2 \f2  Lifts Risk -- Market Talk," at 0700 GMT, misstated the level of 3Q Chinese growth at 7.7%. It should have read 7.3% growth.)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0714 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--The UK is scheduled to sell GBP3 billion 2.75% Sep 2024 gilts at 0930 GMT. The 10-year sector performed strongly amid the risk aversion driven rally last week, with 10-year yields slipping below 2% briefly for the first time since 2013. Since then, gilts have cheapened, consistent with general moves in comparable core bond markets before rallying again yesterday, say analysts at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Barclays\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Regarding relative value, the Sep 24s look cheap on the asset swap curve particularly versus the Mar 25s (the current long gilt future CTD), "which should help generate demand for the bond." The 2.75% Sep 2024 closed Monday at 2.13%. (nick.cawley@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0709 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] \f28 \uc2 \f2 Malaysia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is likely to hold its policy interest rate at 3.25% for the rest of the year amid signs of weakening external demand and moderation in consumption due to accelerating inflation, says a partially government-funded think tank. "There is clearly a need to provide comfort zone, encompassing not only interest rate smoothing and gradual adjustment process, but also providing clear signal that Malaysia needs more than stable consumer prices," says the Malaysian Institute of Economic Research. The think tank notes that "growth outlook matters and inflation can wait a while longer and takes a back seat." MIER forecasts GDP to grow 5.7% in 2014 from 2013's 4.7% while inflation will likely accelerate to 3.5% this year from 2013's 2.1%. (jason.ng@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0700 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--The U.S. dollar drifted lower overnight as U.S. yields fell and equities pushed higher (\f28 \uc2 \f2 S&P\f28 \uc2 \f2  +1%) which gave the market a sentiment lift. In Asia, China data encouraged the risk trades, with the Australian dollar outperforming. China 3Q GDP slowed to 7.3% but was still just above forecast and both industrial production and retail sales came close to expectations. That said the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nikkei\f28 \uc2 \f2  sold off into the close, ending down 2% which triggered late session yen buying. Up ahead U.K. public finance data are due at 0830 GMT and U.S. existing home sales, at 1400 GMT, grab attention. (gary.stride@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Corrections and Amplifications\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 This item was corrected at 07:47 GMT. The original misstated the level of 3Q Chinese growth at 7.7%. It should have read 7.3% growth.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0657 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Indian metal and power stocks rise after the government said late Monday that it will auction 74 coal-mining licenses to private companies in the next three to four months. India is reallocating hundreds of mining licenses after the country's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Supreme Court\f28 \uc2 \f2  last month canceled 214 such licenses issued to private and public companies, saying they were given out in a non-transparent and arbitrary fashion. The new licenses now will be auctioned to private-sector companies but only for captive use, meaning the coal can be only used by the companies and not sold to others. "The ordinance is a first step towards bringing in transparency in coal block auctions and is thus a welcome step," \f28 \uc2 \f2 Motilal Oswal Securities\f28 \uc2 \f2  says. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Jindal Steel & Power\f28 \uc2 \f2  (532286.BY) rises 5.6%, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sesa Sterlite\f28 \uc2 \f2  (500295.BY) gains 4.4%, while \f28 \uc2 \f2 Adani Power\f28 \uc2 \f2  (533096.BY) is up 2.6%. (debiprasad.nayak@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0606 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Despite USD/JPY's fall at close to 105 last week, there is no marked a change in the broader uptrend for the pair, says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Deutsche Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 , citing that the U.S. economy remains on track for over 3% annual growth, and expectation for the gap between U.S. and Japan monetary policy to keep widening. "As long as it does, it's reasonable to look for USD/JPY to maintain its uptrend into 2015," says house strategist Taisuke Tanaka. Japan equities' sharp rally from late August also saw short-term investors go long in Japanese equities, and substantial room for profit-taking here was largely responsible for the market's correction, he adds. Dollar declines as a prime opportunity for dollar buying, he says, predicting USD/JPY to firm at around its current level before re-testing Y110 in the next 1-2 months amid favorable U.S. economic indicators. (bradford.frischkorn@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 October 21, 2014 04:19 ET (08:19 GMT)\f28 \par