\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Rouble hits new low, stocks sag as falling oil burns\b0\par\par\uc2 834 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Oktober 2014\par 11:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 * Russian assets hammered by oil price declines\par \par \uc2 * Gulf bourses also hit\par \par \uc2 * Oil importing nations see stocks rise\par \par \uc2 By Marc Jones\par \par \uc2 LONDON, Oct 15 (Reuters) - Russian and Middle Eastern markets remained under heavy pressure on Wednesday as another dive in oil prices - their main revenue earner - sparked new selling, while slowing global inflation pushed some emerging market bond yields to new lows.\par \par \uc2 As oil slid towards $80 a barrel, the rouble dipped to its weakest level on record, Russian government borrowing costs hovered at a five-year high and shares in Moscow fell to near their lowest level since 2009.\par \par \uc2 It sparked new measures from \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including another shift in its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  threshold and auctions for banks to deposit dollars, but analysts remained sceptical of their success.\par \par \uc2 "If the oil price doesn't stabilise, there probably isn't much hope for the rouble," said Richard Segal, an emerging market strategist at Jefferies. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is down almost 20 percent this year.\par \par \uc2 MSCI's emerging equity share index slipped 0.25 percent following a similar move on Monday. It continued to outperform broader markets, however, as Chinese , Thai and Turkish stocks - all are big oil importers and benefit from price falls - saw gains.\par \par \uc2 Emerging markets have been suffering as the U.S. Federal Reserve prepares to end years of aggressive stimulus and heads towards its first post-crisis rate rise.\par \par \uc2 But there are some signs the rising dollar and the impact of falling oil prices on inflation may cause the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to go easy on policy tightening.\par \par \uc2 U.S. bond yields have collapsed in recent days on that view and government bond yields in Poland and Hungary, which are also pricing in both domestic and euro zone policy easing, hit new lows on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Among other major oil producers, Saudi Arabia saw its stock market lose another 1.7 percent as the bourse heads for its worst week since early 2011. Other Gulf markets also sagged, though Nigerian markets were steadier in west Africa, where the Ebola outbreak has also fuelled concerns.\par \par \uc2 Greek stocks which are now part of most emerging market indexes, fell another 1 percent to take their fall this week to almost 7 percent and bond-yields remained above 7 percent. The moves came as fears grew over whether Greece's fragile conservative-led government can hold on if new elections are called.\par \par \uc2 \f2 Emerging Markets Prices from Reuters            \par  Equities                  Latest    Net Chg  % Chg  % Chg\par               \par               \par on year\par               \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Morgan Stanley\f28 \uc2 \f2                \par  Emrg Mkt Indx    989.60    -2.48   -0.25   -1.31\par               \par Czech Rep            928.54   -10.95   -1.17   -6.12\par               \par Poland           2409.12    +6.22   +0.26   +0.34\par               \par Hungary           17627.37   -50.49   -0.29   -5.05\par               \par Romania           6969.86   +31.19   +0.45   +7.33\par               \par Greece              937.36   -10.85   -1.14  -19.38\par               \par Russia            1063.15   -12.30   -1.14  -23.42\par               \par South Africa   42067.24  -433.71   -1.02   +1.41\par               \par Turkey          75179.42  +492.81   +0.66  +10.88\par               \par China     