\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Russian stocks' rally loses momentum, rouble steadied by  \highlight22\uc2 interventions \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 713 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Oktober 2014\par 18:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 (Adds details, updates prices)\par \par \uc2 By Jason Bush\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Oct 9 (Reuters) - A rally in Russian stocks lost momentum on Thursday and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  steadied the rouble as falling oil prices offset a boost to global sentiment from the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Russian stock indexes had risen around 2 percent in the morning and the rouble firmed against the dollar, as global markets were encouraged by Wednesday's minutes from the U.S. Federal Reserve which suggested it was cautious about raising interest rates.\par \par \uc2 At close the gains were more modest, however. The dollar-based RTS was up 0.6 percent at 1,088 points while the rouble-based MICEX index had risen 0.3 percent.\par \par \uc2 The price of oil, Russia's major export and a key driver for asset prices, resumed its descent after a brief recovery in the morning. Brent fell around 50c to below $91 a barrel.\par \par \uc2 "The chances that (the \uc2 Fed\uc2  minutes) will have a strong influence on the position of the rouble isn't high," said \uc2 Promsvyazbank\uc2  analyst Alexei Egorov.\par \par \uc2 The rouble has been under pressure from Ukraine-related sanctions that have restricted inflows of Western finance.\par \par \uc2 At 1600 GMT the rouble was down 0.3 percent against the dollar at 40.12, and up 0.12 percent at 50.87 versus the euro.\par \par \uc2 The rouble was 0.04 percent weaker at 44.95 against the dollar-euro basket the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  uses to gauge the rouble's nominal exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 The rouble briefly touched 45.02 against the basket, an all-time low. It was steady for most of the day at around 45.95 against the basket, suggesting that it held at the edge of its corridor through \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Traders said that the bank shifted the rouble's corridor twice on Thursday morning and again in the evening, so that the corridor now stretches from 36.00 to 45.00 against the basket.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the rouble within its corridor, but moves the corridor by 5 kopecks each time the bank expends $350 million in \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The bank said on Thursday that it had spent $442 million on Tuesday to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . This follows \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  of $420 million on Monday and $980 million on Friday. Analysts at \uc2 Alfa Bank\uc2  estimated that the bank had made some $1.2 billion on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Analysts at Rosbank said that a deficit of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remained a problem that would weigh on the rouble in the near term, given impending foreign debt repayments and the sanctions.\par \par \uc2 "Our rough rule of thumb shows that the possible size of the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  deficit is in the range from $11 billion to $24 billion," they wrote.\par \par \uc2 "As a result, satisfying the given deficit exclusively through \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  could push (the top of the rouble's corridor) at least to 45.90."\par \par \uc2 Similar conclusions were reached by Raiffeisenbank analysts, who said in a report that "$3 billion from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  isn't enough to compensate for the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  deficit".\par \par \uc2 "The balance of fundamental factors (including the risk of a fall in oil prices), in our view, points towards risks of a further weakening of the rouble."\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  published nine-month balance of payments data on Thursday evening which showed only a modest increase in net capital outflows during the third quarter.\par \par \uc2 The bank said that these outflows totalled $77.5 billion in the first nine months of the year, after adjustment for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps, of which $5.7 billion was in the third quarter.\par \par \uc2 However, analysts are worried about the impact of high foreign debt repayments in the fourth quarter, with over $30 billion due to be repaid in December alone.\par \par \uc2 Russia has lost around a 10th of hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves so far this year in dollar terms, bucking a generally rising trend across most emerging markets.\par \par \uc2 For rouble poll data see\par \par \uc2 For Russian equities guide see\par \par \uc2 For Russian treasury bonds see\par \par \uc2 Russia in graphics: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/dun63s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/dun63s}}}\uc2  (Reporting by Jason Bush, Alexander Winning, Lidia Kelly and Vladimir Abramov; Writing by Jason Bush; Editing by Ruth Pitchford) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-10-9T17:56:27.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020141009eaa900af4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
