\par\par \b \uc2 FACTBOX-Dollar surge forces central banks to tap reserves\b0\par\par\uc2 1,409 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Oktober 2014\par 14:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 * Graphic on world's \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/jyx68s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/jyx68s}}}\par \par \uc2 * Graphic on emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/peb85s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/peb85s}}}\par \par \uc2 * Article on cbanks' euro reserve holdings\par \par \uc2 By Anirban Nag and Sujata Rao\par \par \uc2 LONDON, Oct 8 (Reuters) - The U.S. dollar's recent surge to four-year highs has forced central banks across the world to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on open markets to prevent their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  falling too sharply.\par \par \uc2 As the \uc2 Fed\uc2  ends its asset purchase programme this month and investors brace for higher U.S. interest rates next year, yields on \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  bonds have climbed relative to those of other governments. Dollar-funded 'carry trades' - where traders borrow in low interest \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy higher yielding but riskier assets - are also being rapidly unwound.\par \par \uc2 As pressure on dollar exchange rates mounts, dollar-priced commodities have fallen and U.S.-based investments in many emerging markets are being rethought.\par \par \uc2 To stem that flight and prevent steep local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  losses feeding inflation and hampering foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  debt servicing, central banks from Russia to South Korea and Indonesia to Turkey have stepped up the sale of dollar cash reserves.\par \par \uc2 Ever since the dollar's rise accelerated in July, global \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves have started to fall from record highs recorded by the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  at mid-year.\par \par \uc2 The IMF data, released this week, showed \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  holdings of global central banks at a record $12 trillion in the second quarter of this year, up from $11.859 trillion in the first three months of the year.\par \par \uc2 However, the surge of the dollar index by 7.7 percent in the third quarter has been met with heavy sales of dollar reserves. The index has risen for 12 weeks, its longest winning streak in four decades. ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\par \par \uc2 US dollar index's consecutive weekly gains/losses since 1971\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/sek92w"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/sek92w}}}\par \par \uc2 10Y Bund/Treasury spread vs \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  - last 30 years\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/qeh92w"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/qeh92w}}}\uc2  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\par \par \uc2 Here is what some countries are doing to tackle the dollar's strength and details on their \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves: -----------------------------------\par \par \uc2 SOUTH KOREA\par \par \uc2 South Korean authorities have been seen selling dollars through September to prop up the won, which is trading near six-month lows against the dollar. Data show its foreign reserves fell for the first time in 14 months in August to $367.5 billion, and declined by $3.13 billion in September to $364.41 billion.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 RUSSIA\b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the rouble, spending a combined $1.4 billion on Oct. 3 and Oct. 6. It has also moved the rouble's floating corridor several times - it stands now at 35.65-44.65 against a dollar-euro basket . Russia's gold and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves have fallen sharply in recent months, standing at $456.8 billion on Oct. 2, down from $475.8 billion at the end of June.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is down almost 18 percent this year versus the dollar, as Western sanctions over the conflict in Ukraine push Russia's economy towards recession and capital flight estimates mount.\par \par \uc2 TURKEY\par \par \uc2 The lira is trading at an eight-month low against the dollar. \uc2 Turkey's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has increased the amount of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  available at daily auctions to a minimum of $40 million from $10 million and left interest rates on hold last week. Turkey's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserve assets stood at $111.3 billion, down from $133 billion at mid-year.\par \par \uc2 BRAZIL\par \par \uc2 The real fell to near six-year lows against the dollar in late September but has recovered some ground after the first election round on Oct. 5 showed a surge in support for pro-business candidate Aecio Neves.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had stepped up its support for the real via \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap contracts - derivatives that emulate the sale of dollars in futures markets. Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves were at $375.7 billion at the end of September, down from $380.5 billion in June.\par \par \uc2 INDIA\par \par \uc2 The Indian rupee fell to seven-month lows last week, with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cited as selling dollars to prop up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Official \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves data showed totals of $314 billion as of Sept. 26, down from $315.8 billion at end-June 2014.\par \par \uc2 SOUTH AFRICA\par \par \uc2 The rand has fallen almost 7 percent against the dollar this year. \uc2 The South African Reserve Bank\uc2 , which has already lifted its benchmark interest rate by 75 basis points in 2014, is expected to raise rates again in November. South African \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, which are relatively low, have fallen only slightly to $41.879 billion, however, as the bank tends not to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the rand.\par \par \uc2 NIGERIA\par \par \uc2 Nigeria's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been selling dollars at twice-weekly auctions to help the naira, which recently traded at three-year lows. On Sept. 29, the bank increased the amount of dollars it offered to sell to $500 million, up from $350 million it has offered in the past quarter. Nigeria's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves fell to $39.56 billion by Sept. 26, from $37.5 billion at the end of June.\par \par \uc2 INDONESIA\par \par \uc2 The rupiah has fallen to seven-month lows versus the dollar this week, forcing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell dollars. \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Agus Martowardojo said this week that the bank was prepared to carry out "measured \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 " to keep the rupiah in a range it was comfortable with. Indonesia had reserves worth $111.2 billion at the end of September, compared with $107.7 billion in June 2014.\par \par \uc2 CHINA\par \par \uc2 Beijing has, by some distance, the world's largest share of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, but as the dollar rises broadly there will be less need for the \uc2 Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to mop up the greenback and keep the yuan from strengthening. At the end of the second quarter, China's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves had risen to nearly $4 trillion, according to \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 PERU\par \par \uc2 Peru's sol \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has fallen to the lowest level in almost five years, forcing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell dollars in the spot market. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold $10 million on Tuesday, the latest of several \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent weeks.\par \par \uc2 CHILE\par \par \uc2 Chile's year-long monetary easing cycle is approaching its end, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief Rodrigo Vergara said recently. The peso has depreciated about 12 percent this year versus the dollar, making imports more expensive and driving up inflation. Vergara said the weak peso was "absolutely not a problem".\par \par \uc2 DEVELOPED MARKET ACTIVITY\par \par \uc2 -------------------------\par \par \uc2 JAPAN\par \par \uc2 Japanese Prime Minister Shinzo Abe spoke about the disadvantages of a weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in parliament on Tuesday. Abe said a weaker yen burdens households and small firms by pushing up their fuel costs. His comments come as has faced criticism in parliament over the slide in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  pumps out yen in a bid to stimulate inflation.\par \par \uc2 The dollar rose above 110 yen for the first time since August 2008 last week, continuing to ride on bullish momentum against its peers, given a string of robust U.S. data.\par \par \uc2 SWITZERLAND\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  last month repeated its pledge to buy "unlimited" quantities of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent the franc from strengthening past the limit of 1.20 per euro imposed by the SNB three years ago.\par \par \uc2 The SNB's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend that level has bloated its balance sheet to nearly 500 billion francs. \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves stood at 462.194 billion francs at end September, up from 453.875 billion in August. It has not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the past two years, but with the euro weakening, the SNB's resolve is likely to be put to the test.\par \par \uc2 NEW ZEALAND\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Reserve Bank of New Zealand\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in August for the first time in more than a year to counter the New Zealand dollar's strength. The RBNZ had been cranking up the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rhetoric since July, and chose to act just as the U.S. dollar was rising appreciably, thereby magnifying the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 's impact. The RBNZ sold a net NZ$521 million in August, its biggest sale of local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  since March 2011. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's power may be limited though - daily trade in the "kiwi" is around $100 billion, and its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  war chest is only around $7.5 billion. (Additional reporting by Jamie McGeever; Editing by Andrew Heavens and Susan Fenton) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-10-8T13:22:23.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020141008eaa800dij\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
