\par\par \b \uc2 Russian  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Props Up Ruble\b0\par\par\uc2 By Andrey Ostroukh \par \uc2 357 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Oktober 2014\par 09:44\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW--The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to shore up the ruble, shifting the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's trading corridor again following its drop to record lows Monday on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, according to latest data from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  shifted the ruble's corridor 10 kopecks higher to 35.60 rubles to 44.60 rubles versus the euro-dollar basket on Monday, data released Tuesday from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  showed.\par \par \uc2 The move suggests that the Bank of Russia spent at least $700 million on the first trading day of the week to prop up the ruble.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  keeps the ruble within a floating trading band and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the ruble weakens to the upper boundary of the band. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sells $350 million at the upper boundary and then shifts the ruble's band by five kopecks higher. If the ruble weakens to the band's edge again, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  with another $350 million from its reserves.\par \par \uc2 The ruble has come under intense downside pressure in the past month.\par \par \uc2 Sliding oil prices have hit Russia's economic hard given the country's dependence on oil and gas exports.\par \par \uc2 At the same time, sanctions imposed by Western countries after Russia's annexation of Crimea and support for rebels in eastern Ukraine have limited the ability of Russian banks and companies to borrow abroad.\par \par \uc2 Unable to fund themselves on Western markets, Russian firms and lenders are buying more dollars and euros on the local market.\par \par \uc2 The ruble's most recent slump in value triggered \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in early October, the first time since May. Since the beginning of this month, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  shifted the trading band by a cumulative 20 kopecks.\par \par \uc2 The ruble hovered at 44.41 versus the euro-dollar basket in early Tuesday trading in Moscow, outside the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level.\par \par \uc2 Against the U.S. itself, the ruble traded at 39.70, just above its all-time low of 40.05 hit overnight.\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 October 07, 2014 03:44 ET (07:44 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020141007eaa7000o4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
