\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Russian  \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes \highlight\uc2  after rouble breaches trading band\b0\par\par\uc2 558 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Oktober 2014\par 15:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 (Updates to reflect afternoon trading, adds comments)\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Oct 7 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the rouble on Tuesday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  again breached the bank's trading band, as companies starved of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  because of sanctions continued to show robust demand for dollars.\par \par \uc2 The Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been battered for months by falling oil prices and risk aversion towards Moscow-listed assets due to the crisis in Ukraine, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has repeatedly defended the rouble in the past week.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  automatically \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the edges of the rouble's trading band against a dollar-euro basket, which stretched from 35.60 to 44.60 as of Monday. Once it spends $350 million defending the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  shifts the band by 5 kopecks.\par \par \uc2 "Judging by the prices, the corridor was moved (again today). This was caused by the resumption of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Igor Akinshin, a \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at \uc2 Alfa Bank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The local demand for foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is constant, but yesterday people sold the dollar given world trends. We also had dollar sales yesterday once it reached the 40 (roubles to the dollar) mark. But that's all been bought up, and now the market is going back to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Akinshin said.\par \par \uc2 Western sanctions shutting major Russian banks and firms out of international capital markets have driven sharply higher demand for overseas \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which large Russian firms need to meet external debt obligations.\par \par \uc2 The rouble was trading 0.48 percent weaker at 39.92 against the dollar at 1305 GMT, close to an all-time low touched on Monday.\par \par \uc2 It was down 0.18 percent at 50.37 versus the euro . That left the rouble 0.33 percent lower at 44.62 against the dollar-euro basket the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  uses to gauge the rouble's nominal exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has shifted the rouble's trading band by at least 20 kopecks since Friday.. It said on Tuesday it had spent $980 million defending the rouble on Oct. 3 but is yet to release data for the amount it has spent since the start of the week.\par \par \uc2 Russian shares also lost ground on Tuesday, reversing strong gains of over 2 percent made in the previous session.\par \par \uc2 "Yesterday's rise was clearly driven by people closing short positions, but after that the market started to slip back under its own momentum. I don't see any signal for purchases yet," said Alexei Surov, an equities trader at \uc2 Bank Zenit\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 By 1305 GMT the dollar-denominated RTS index was down 1 percent to 1,108 points, while the rouble-based MICEX was down 0.9 percent at 1,404 points.\par \par \uc2 Top bank \uc2 Sberbank\uc2  fell 1 percent, while state oil producer Rosneft was up 0.1 percent.\par \par \uc2 Oil, one of Russia's chief exports, edged lower on Tuesday, with the front-month futures contract for benchmark Brent trading around $92.5 per barrel.\par \par \uc2 For rouble poll data see\par \par \uc2 For Russian equities guide see\par \par \uc2 For Russian treasury bonds see\par \par \uc2 Russia in graphics: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/dun63s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/dun63s}}}\uc2  (Reporting by Vladimir Abramov and Zlata Garasyuta; Writing by Alexander Winning and Lidia Kelly; Editing by \uc2 Alison Williams\uc2 ) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-10-7T14:16:41.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020141007eaa700crd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
