\par\par \b \uc2 Russian Ruble, Stocks Continue To Tumble -- Barron's Blog\b0\par\par\uc2 By Dimitra DeFotis   \par \uc2 360 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 September 2014\par 15:32\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The ruble continued a six-day losing streak Monday after dropping to its worst valuation since the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was restructured in 1998.\par \par \uc2 Contributing: the threat of more sanctions against Russia looms. Talks between the presidents of Russia and Ukraine didn't yield much, and this morning there's more talk about \uc2 NATO\uc2  troops protecting the Baltic states. Add to that \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has pledged to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  less in ruble valuation.\par \par \uc2 Bloomberg reports today:\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell 0.3 percent [... against] the dollar to 37.4180 at 2:41 p.m. in Moscow. The yield on 10-year local-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds dropped two basis points to 9.81 percent after reaching the highest since Aug. 8 yesterday. gained 0.2 percent to 1,394.45, rising for the first time in four days, after an earlier retreat of 0.4 percent."\par \par \uc2 The BBC reported last week that:\par \par \uc2 "\uc2 Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said earlier this month it would abolish from next year a so-called trading corridor, which limits its swing in value against \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the dollar and euro. Russia has more than $400 billion of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves. When its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is weak, it can spend dollars to purchase roubles in the market to shore up the value ..."\par \par \uc2 Today, the Russian-traded shares of \uc2 Sberbank\uc2  Rossia ( SBRCY) are down 0.73%. Shares of oil giant Lukoil( LUKOY) were flat on the Russia exchange, while shares of natural gas player \uc2 Gazprom\uc2  ( OGZPY) were down slightly.\par \par \uc2 The Market Vectors Russia ETF ( RSX) fell nearly 2% Friday and the \uc2 iShares MSCI Russia Capped ETF\uc2  ( ERUS) dropped more than 2 percentage points. As for trading vehicles: the Direxion Daily Russia Bear 3X Shares ( RUSS) rose 5.7% Friday, while the Direxion Daily Russia Bull 3X Shares ( RUSL) fell 5.7%. The market decline in Russia has been a drag on the iShares MSCI Poland ETF ( EPOL), which was off by nearly 0.3% Friday. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  More at Barron's Emerging Markets blog, \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://blogs.barrons.com/emergingmarketsdaily/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://blogs.barrons.com/emergingmarketsdaily/}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 September 02, 2014 09:32 ET (13:32 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140902ea92001sv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
