\par\par \b \uc2 Ruble Plumbs New Depth as Ukraine Tensions Rise\b0\par\par\uc2 By Andrey Ostroukh and Chiara Albanese \par \uc2 470 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 August 2014\par 14:54\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires Chinese (English)\par \uc2 RTNW\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW--The Russian ruble hit a new low on Friday as geopolitical conflict in eastern Ukraine intensified with the alleged participation of Russian troops.\par \par \uc2 Kiev said that Russian troops entered eastern regions of Ukraine in support of pro-Russian rebels. Moscow denied the claim that Russia now has a military presence in the neighboring country.\par \par \uc2 "Against the backdrop [of military \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ] I want to stay away from those assets affected by the mounting geopolitical risks. That includes the ruble," said Benoit Anne, emerging-market strategist at \uc2 Soci\u233\'00\'E9t\u233\'00\'E9 G\u233\'00\'E9n\u233\'00\'E9rale\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 At the market opening, the ruble briefly eased to 37.02 versus the dollar, losing 0.7% on the day. That took the ruble below its previous record of 37 per dollar, which it hit on the first trading day of March after the West had threatened to punish Moscow for its annexation of Crimea.\par \par \uc2 The ruble soon pulled back below 37 versus the dollar, hovering around 36.92. But the Russian unit could plumb new depths should the crisis in Ukraine escalate further as foreign players are the main sellers of the ruble, \uc2 Nordea Bank\uc2  said in a research note.\par \par \uc2 In March, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped in with higher \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets and raised interest rates in an emergency move to stem the ruble's descent, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  isn't taking part in the market anymore.\par \par \uc2 In mid-August the bank widened the ruble exchange-rate corridor and scrapped all \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  within it. Although the move was a part of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's longtime goal of switching to an inflation-targeting policy, scheduled for 2015, it deprived the ruble of any state support at times of increased pressure.\par \par \uc2 The approach of end-of-month tax payments, which prompt export-focused companies to convert foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  so they can meet local liabilities, also plays against the ruble, which has nearly become a free-float \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 While the ruble is the worst performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar on the day, the increasingly sour tones between Russia and Ukraine are taking their toll on neighboring \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as well.\par \par \uc2 The Polish zloty was trading at its weakest level against the euro in around six months Friday, with a euro worth 4.2349 zloty.\par \par \uc2 "In a case scenario of military confrontation between Russia and the West, all bets will be off and the euro could appreciate above 4.30 against the zloty," said \uc2 rabobank\uc2  strategist Piotr Matys.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the Ukrainian hryvnia is trading around 13.49 against the dollar, recovering slightly from Thursday's record just below 14.\par \par \uc2 Write to Andrey Ostroukh at andrey.ostroukh@wsj.com and Chiara Albanese at chiara.albanese@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 29-08-14 1254GMT\par \par \uc2 Dokument RTNW000020140829ea8t0009k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
