\par\par \b \uc2 As  \highlight22\uc2 Russia Intervenes \highlight\uc2 , Ruble, Bonds Strengthen -- Barron's Blog\b0\par\par\uc2 By Dimitra DeFotis   \par \uc2 264 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 August 2014\par 18:21\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Pushing to show confidence in the face of conflict in Ukraine, Russia widened the ruble's trading band Monday.\par \par \uc2 The move is a step toward a free float of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Bloomberg reports that:\par \par \uc2 "Policy makers increased the corridor to 9 rubles from 7 rubles and abandoned \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  within the band, according to a statement on the Bank of Russia website Monday. The ruble strengthened 0.3 percent to 41.5176 against the bank's target basket of dollars and euros late Monday in Moscow. The yield on 10-year government bonds rose one basis point to 9.28 percent, reversing five days of declines. The changes are intended to help complete the shift to a freely-floating ruble by the end of the year. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  intends to focus on inflation targeting and interest rates in its policy, rather than \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Among \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 -focused exchange-traded funds; The Market Vectors \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  ETF ( RSX) and the iShares MSCIRussia Capped ETF ( ERUS) are each up more than 2%. As for trading vehicles tied to Russia markets: the Direxion Daily Russia Bear 3X Shares ( RUSS) fell more than 6% and the Direxion Daily Russia Bull 3X Shares ( RUSL) rose more than 6%.\par \par \uc2 Russia is outpacing other emerging markets today. A broader measure of emerging markets, the iShares MSCI Core Emerging Markets ETF ( IEMG) is up 0.7%. \par \par \uc2 \f2 