\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Financial Services News of the Day\b0\par\par\uc2 564 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Juni 2014\par 22:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FINANCIAL SERVICES TOP STORIES \par  \par U.S. REACHES $968 MILLION SETTLEMENT WITH SUNTRUST \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SunTrust Banks\f28 \uc2 \f2  reached a $968 million agreement with the \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. government\f28 \uc2 \f2  to settle allegations of abusive mortgage lending and servicing practices. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CITIGROUP \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  CHIEF JEFF FEIG TO LEAVE BANK \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The departure of Jeff Feig, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Citigroup\f28 \uc2 \f2 's global head of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , follows that of the firm's most senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  banker, Anil Prasad, earlier this year. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par IFC SELLS FIRST OFFSHORE RENMINBI BOND TO FUND GREEN PROJECTS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 International Finance Corporation\f28 \uc2 \f2 , part of \f28 \uc2 \f2 the World Bank Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 , sold the first ever offshore renminbi bond designed to fund environmentally friendly projects. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 DEUTSCHE BANK\f28 \uc2 \f2  HIRES SYLVIE MATHERAT AS REGULATORY HEAD \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Germany's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Deutsche Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  said it had hired Sylvie Matherat from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 French \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as its new global head of regulatory affairs. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 OMERS\f28 \uc2 \f2  ADDS TRADER FROM MACQUARIE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Canadian pension fund \f28 \uc2 \f2 OMERS\f28 \uc2 \f2  has hired program trader Bilal Ijaz, a spokeswoman for the fund confirmed. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ING'S INSURANCE FLOAT MAY LACK BUOYANCY \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ING's insurance arm, which is being floated as penance for state aid the bank took during the financial crisis, has been priced to sell. But big uncertainties remain over what investors will get over the medium term. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JEFFERIES GROUP PROFIT RISES 55% \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Jefferies reported a profit of $61.3 million as the firm reported strong results in its investment-banking and equities-trading units, outweighing a drop in fixed income trading revenue.Net revenue increased 9.8% to $723 million. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SUPREME COURT REJECTS ARGENTINA DEBT CASE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Supreme Court\f28 \uc2 \f2  handed Argentina a major setback in its long-running battle with a small group of determined creditors, heightening the risk the country will default for the second time in 13 years. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FLOWS RETURN TO EMERGING MARKETS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A fresh wave of investment inflows is taking the pressure off some emerging-market governments that had at long last started to tackle economic overhauls, write Michael S. Arnold, Patrick McGroarty and Emre Peker. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ECB EXTENDS DOLLAR LIQUIDITY BEYOND JULY \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said it will continue to offer one-week U.S. dollar liquidity-providing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  beyond the end of July. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par LSE SIGNS PACT WITH BANK OF CHINA \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 London Stock Exchange\f28 \uc2 \f2  said it has signed a pact with Bank of China to promote the development of an offshore Renminbi market in the U.K. BoC would also work towards becoming an LSE member. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par U.K. INFLATION DROPS DESPITE FASTER GROWTH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Annual inflation in the U.K. slowed in May to its lowest rate in almost five years, a sign that price pressures remain subdued despite a rapid pickup in growth. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA PBOC OFFERS $4.8 BILLION 28-DAY REPOS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is offering $4.8 billion worth of 28-day repurchase agreements in open-market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , traders participating in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par RUSSIA TO LET RUBLE FLOAT FROM 2015 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Russia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said it is cutting \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  aimed at smoothing ruble volatility, partially removing a defense implemented in early March before Moscow annexed Crimea. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SWEDEN SEES LOWER BORROWING AS ECONOMY STRENGTHENS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Swedish National Debt Office\f28 \uc2 \f2  has reduced its forecast for the country's net borrowing requirement in 2014 and 2015 as the strengthening economy is leading to faster-than-expected increases in tax income.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 June 17, 2014 16:00 ET (20:00 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140617ea6h0036b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
