\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 337 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Juni 2014\par 11:33\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 EURO-ZONE WAGES SLOW, JOB OPENINGS RISE\par \par \uc2 Euro-zone wage growth slowed in the first three months of this year, while total labor costs also rose at a more sluggish pace, both signs that inflationary pressures in the euro zone were weakening.\par \par \uc2 U.K. INFLATION DROPS DESPITE FASTER GROWTH\par \par \uc2 Annual inflation in the U.K. slowed in May to its lowest rate in almost five years, a sign that price pressures remain subdued despite a rapid pickup in growth.\par \par \uc2 ECB EXTENDS DOLLAR LIQUIDITY BEYOND JULY\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it will continue to offer one-week U.S. dollar liquidity-providing \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  beyond the end of July.\par \par \uc2 SWEDEN SEES LOWER BORROWING AS ECONOMY STRENGTHENS\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Swedish National Debt Office\uc2  has reduced its forecast for the country's net borrowing requirement in 2014 and 2015 as the strengthening economy is leading to faster-than-expected increases in tax income.\par \par \uc2 IEA SEES SPREAD OF SHALE REVOLUTION\par \par \uc2 The U.S. shale boom will spread beyond North America before the end of the decade, sooner than previously expected, the \uc2 International Energy Agency\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA TO LET RUBLE FLOAT FROM 2015\par \par \uc2 The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it is cutting \b \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  aimed at smoothing ruble volatility, partially removing a defense implemented in early March before Moscow annexed Crimea.\par \par \uc2 CHINA MAY FOREIGN DIRECT INVESTMENT FALLS\par \par \uc2 China attracted $8.6 billion of foreign direct investment in May, down 6.7% from a year earlier, the Ministry of Commerce said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 CHINA PBOC OFFERS $4.8 BILLION 28-DAY REPOS\par \par \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is offering $4.8 billion worth of 28-day repurchase agreements in open-market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders participating in the \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 AUSTRALIA \b \highlight22\uc2 CENTRAL BANK\b0 \highlight\uc2  FELT LOW RATES STILL NEEDED\par \par \uc2 Australia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sees the nation's economy remaining sluggish this year, and considers that record-low interest rates are needed to support it for some time.\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 June 17, 2014 05:33 ET (09:33 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140617ea6h000x3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
