\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Russia \highlight\uc2  Trims  \highlight22\uc2 Currency Interventions \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Andrey Ostroukh \par \uc2 512 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Mai 2014\par 09:41\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Thursday it cut the amount of daily \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , aimed at limiting ruble volatility, moving closer to inflation targeting.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  plans to let the ruble float freely starting from 2015 and instead focus on taming inflation through interest rates.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , however, retains a right to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if it deems it necessary for financial stability. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which keeps the ruble within a floating band against the euro-dollar basket, said it trimmed the amount of daily \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by $100 million.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sells foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the ruble weakens toward the upper boundary of the trading corridor, and buys dollars and euros when the ruble closes in on the lower boundary of the band.\par \par \uc2 It carries out no \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the middle of the trading band.\par \par \uc2 The ruble showed muted reaction to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  decision, adding 0.25% on the day and hovering at 39.94 against the euro-dollar basket in the no-\b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  range. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a news release the decision to trim \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  shouldn't have any impact on the Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Write to Andrey Ostroukh at andrey.ostroukh@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 22 May 2014 06:25 ET  \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  Trims Daily \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency Interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  -- Update\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par By Andrey Ostroukh \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Russia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Thursday it cut the amount of daily \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , aimed at limiting ruble volatility, moving closer to inflation targeting.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  plans to let the ruble float freely starting from 2015 and instead focus on taming inflation through interest rates.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , however, retains a right to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  if it deems it necessary for financial stability. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which keeps the ruble within a floating band against the euro-dollar basket, said it trimmed the amount of daily \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by $100 million.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sells foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  when the ruble weakens toward the upper boundary of the trading corridor, and buys dollars and euros when the ruble closes in on the lower boundary of the band. It carries out no \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the middle of the trading band.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 While the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been scaling down daily \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , it stands ready to protect the ruble from excessive weakening and will sell $1.5 billion from reserves if the ruble slides to the upper boundary of a trading corridor against a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  basket made up of dollars and euros.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Previously, before the March selloff, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was selling $350 million on the band's upper boundary before shifting the band higher by 5 kopecks.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The ruble showed muted reaction to the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  decision Thursday, adding 0.25% on the day and hovering at 39.94 against the euro-dollar basket in the no-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  range. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said in a news release the decision to trim \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  shouldn't have any impact on the Russian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Andrey Ostroukh at andrey.ostroukh@wsj.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 May 22, 2014 06:25 ET (10:25 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140522ea5m0019m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
