\par\par \b \uc2 Russian stocks mixed on Ukraine election fears, rouble stronger\b0\par\par\uc2 474 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Mai 2014\par 10:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, May 22 (Reuters) - Russian stock indexes were mixed on Thursday morning as upcoming elections in restive Ukraine prompted investor caution, while the rouble continued to strengthen supported by monthly taxes.\par \par \uc2 The rouble-denominated MICEX index was down 0.3 percent by 0725 GMT at 1,435 points, while the dollar-based RTS index had risen less than 0.1 percent to 1,317 points.\par \par \uc2 The RTS was supported by the firmer rouble, which touched a four-month high against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 "The prospect of elections in Ukraine is adding an element of nervousness to the market," said Oleg Shagov, chief analyst at \uc2 Promsvyazbank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The West has threatened tougher sanctions against Russia if it disrupts the election. Western countries have accused Russia of tacitly supporting separatists in two eastern Ukraine regions, who have vowed to prevent the elections taking place in their regions.\par \par \uc2 "Meanwhile, the market has returned to the level it reached before President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  received parliamentary approval to send troops to Ukraine, and there's clearly resistance at this level," Shagov said.\par \par \uc2 Gains in global oil benchmark Brent and optimism stemming from gains in broader global markets checked further losses.\par \par \uc2 The oil price is a key determinant of profits at Russian energy companies, which have some of the largest market capitalisations on domestic stock markets.\par \par \uc2 However, the share price of \uc2 Gazprom\uc2 , which signed a massive deal to supply China with gas on Wednesday, was down 0.5 percent.\par \par \uc2 "We deem the (implicit gas supply) price to be low and view the contract as negative for \uc2 Gazprom\uc2 's valuation. In our opinion, the euphoria surrounding the contract and the stock rally has come to an end, and we are struggling to identify any additional positive triggers for \uc2 Gazprom\uc2  in the near-term," \uc2 Alfa Bank\uc2  analyst Alexander Kornilov said in a note.\par \par \uc2 In \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, the rouble strengthened in advance of the end-of-month tax period that requires Russian exporters to convert foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  into roubles to pay taxes.\par \par \uc2 The rouble touched a three-month high against the dollar-euro basket, strengthening 0.1 percent to 39.98 by 0725 GMT.\par \par \uc2 The Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  firmed 0.19 percent against the dollar to 34.28 and 0.36 percent against the euro to 46.84.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced it had reduced the size of its daily \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by $100 million for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  ranges within the rouble's floating corridor.\par \par \uc2 The move reflects an easing of market turmoil linked to fears of Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Ukraine and \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's annexation of Crimea in March.\par \par \uc2 For rouble poll data see\par \par \uc2 For Russian equities guide see\par \par \uc2 For Russian treasury bonds see\par \par \uc2 Russia in graphics: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/dun63s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/dun63s}}}\uc2  (Reporting by Alexander Winning; Editing by Toby Chopra)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-5-25T08:05:14.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140522ea5m008hy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
