\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Russian  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  reduces size of daily  \highlight22\uc2 interventions \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 458 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Mai 2014\par 09:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds detail, background)\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, May 22 (Reuters) - The \uc2 Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has cut the size of the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  it carries out to support the rouble, signalling a return to its strategy of allowing the rouble to float more freely.\par \par \uc2 The move reflects an easing of market turmoil linked to fears of Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Ukraine and \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's annexation of Crimea in March.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced it had reduced the size of its daily \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by $100 million for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  ranges within the rouble's floating corridor.\par \par \uc2 The bank said the change was made in order to increase the flexibility of the rouble in preparation for an inflation targeting regime.\par \par \uc2 Previously the bank had spent $400 million a day when the rouble was trading within 95 kopecks of the upper edge of the top range of the corridor, or $200 million when it was trading in a range of one rouble below that.\par \par \uc2 These amounts will now be reduced to $300 million and $100 million respectively.\par \par \uc2 The corridor is seven roubles wide and currently stretches from 36.40 to 43.40 against the basket. The rouble is now trading near the middle of the corridor where the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  carries out no \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The bank aims to adopt inflation targeting from the start of next year, a policy framework that envisages allowing the rouble to float, while controlling interest rates more tightly.\par \par \uc2 However, this strategy received a setback in March, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  introduced measures to control the rouble more tightly, reacting to a sharp sell-off provoked by the crisis in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 One of the steps introduced in March was to increase the size of accumulated \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , needed to provoke a shift in the floating corridor, from $350 million to $1.5 billion, making such shifts much less frequent.\par \par \uc2 In its statement on Thursday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the $1.5 billion threshold would remain in place for now.\par \par \uc2 This means that although the rouble will now become more flexible within its corridor, the corridor itself is not being made more flexible. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  carries out unlimited \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the rouble is at the edge of the corridor.\par \par \uc2 The rouble strengthened slightly after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announcement before falling back.\par \par \uc2 At 0655 GMT it was trading at 39.95 against the basket, 0.23 percent stronger on the day.\par \par \uc2 The rouble has gained some 3 percent during May, as markets react positively to an easing in international tensions around Ukraine, giving the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  more scope to resume its policy of gradually withdrawing support for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . (Reporting By Jason Bush, editing by Elizabeth Piper)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-5-25T07:04:15.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140522ea5m007vg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\