\par\par \b \uc2 POLL-Rouble set to hit further record low on Ukraine crisis\b0\par\par\uc2 548 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Mai 2014\par 16:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * For poll data see\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate hike boost to rouble only temporary\par \par \uc2 * Rouble to weaken further vs dollar to new record lows\par \par \uc2 * Lira and rand seen mostly steady\par \par \uc2 By Rahul Karunakar and Diptarka Roy\par \par \uc2 May 7 (Reuters) - Russia's rouble will fall to new lows against the dollar over the coming year as the risk of more serious conflict in Ukraine sends investors fleeing, a Reuters poll found.\par \par \uc2 Expectations of economic and financial sanctions against Moscow for its role in the current crisis engulfing Ukraine has caused a sell-off across Russian financial assets.\par \par \uc2 "The risks of further sanctions are high, and they are another rouble negative on top of a long list," wrote Koon Chow, head of emerging markets strategy at \uc2 Barclays\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The rouble, currently trading at 35.40 per dollar, is already the worst-performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year, 8 percent lower against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The consensus from a poll of 35 strategists this week is for it to hit 36.0 per dollar in a month and 36.78 in a year, which would mark its weakest rate since being devalued in the aftermath of Russia's 1998 debt default.\par \par \uc2 In March it fell to a record low 36.57, prompting the \uc2 Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to hike interest rates by a combined 200 basis points to stem \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculation and capital flight.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  popped up 3 percent after that. But it is set to fall again.\par \par \uc2 The economy is already paying for \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Ukraine, with a host of sanctions that have provoked large-scale capital outflows.\par \par \uc2 A separate Reuters poll of economists predicts hard times ahead for Russia, driven by an expected slump in investment.\par \par \uc2 "We feel the worsening growth outlook in Russia leaves little room for further (rate) hikes," said \uc2 Barclays\uc2 ' Koon Chow.\par \par \uc2 "Domestic confidence in the rouble seems to have weakened with reports that the banking system has recently suffered some outflows and that the economy may be slipping into a recession," he said.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2 , which says Russia is already in recession, the \uc2 World Bank\uc2  and the \uc2 Organisation for Economic Co-\b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Development\uc2  have all cut their growth forecasts for Russia.\par \par \uc2 The latest Reuters \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  poll also predicted that Turkey's lira, which has stabilised after a free fall that similarly triggered an aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate rise earlier in the year, will continue to hold steady.\par \par \uc2 The lira, which lost about a fifth of its value in 2013, has gained a little over 2 percent so far this year, and is expected to trade at 2.15 to the dollar in a month, compared with 2.20 in the previous poll. It was last trading at 2.10.\par \par \uc2 It is expected to trade at 2.19 per dollar in three months and settle at 2.23 a dollar in a year, compared to 2.23 and 2.25 per dollar in the previous poll.\par \par \uc2 The South African rand also is expected to trade on a steady path.\par \par \uc2 (For other stories from the Reuters \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  poll ) (Polling and analysis by Swati Chaturvedi and Deepti Govind; Additonal reporting by Seda Sezer and Vuyani Ndaba; Editing by Ruth Pitchford) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-5-7T15:12:31.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140507ea5700r0b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
