\par\par \b \uc2 *Bank of Russia Sells $22.3B, EUR2.3B to Prop Up Ruble in March\b0\par\par\uc2 376 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 April 2014\par 08:47\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Corrections & Amplifications\par \par \uc2 This headline was corrected at 0459 GMT to fix the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , not $2.3B Euro.\par \par \uc2 2 Apr 2014 02:49 ET *\b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 FX Interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in March Highest Since Jan 2009\par \par \uc2 2 Apr 2014 02:49 ET *Ruble Firms 2% Vs Dollar in March After Hitting Record Low on March 3\par \par \uc2 2 Apr 2014 02:56 ET *Russia Finance Minister: To Resume \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Purchases for Reserve Fund in Coming Days\par \par \uc2 2 Apr 2014 02:57 ET *CORRECT: Bank of Russia Sells $22.3B, EUR2.3B to Prop Up Ruble in March\par \par \uc2 2 Apr 2014 03:21 ET  \uc2 Russian Finance Ministry\uc2  to Resume Buying Foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 Currencies\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 By Andrey Ostroukh\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW--\uc2 Russia's finance ministry\uc2  will resume buying foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to replenish the rainy-day reserve fund in the coming days, Finance Minister Anton Siluanov said Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 In early March, when the ruble hit its record lows following threats of sanctions from the West in response to developments in Ukraine, the finance ministry stopped buying foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the reserve fund.\par \par \uc2 The finance ministry had been buying 3.5 billion rubles ($99.8 million) of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the open market daily from Feb. 20. It halted purchases on March 4 to ease downside pressure on the ruble.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  instead increased its presence on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and sold $22.3 billion and 2.3 billion euros ($3.2 billion) in \b \highlight22\uc2 forex interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the ruble. \b \highlight22\uc2 Interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in March, which became the highest since January 2009, helped the ruble to recover from its all-time low of 37 against the dollar and to firm by 2% against the greenback.\par \par \uc2 Write to Andrey Ostroukh at andrey.ostroukh@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 Corrections and Amplifications\par \par \uc2 This item was corrected at 07:31 GMT. The original misstated the ministry in the headline. It should say the finance ministry, not foreign ministry.\par \par \uc2 2 Apr 2014 03:30 ET  Correction to Russia to Resume Buying Foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 Currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  Story\par \par \uc2 ("\uc2 Russian Foreign Ministry\uc2  to Resume Buying Foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 Currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," at 0721 GMT, misstated the ministry in the headline. It should say the finance ministry.\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 April 02, 2014 03:30 ET (07:30 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140402ea42000ls\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
